window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b047-06ac115f4c830004.json"]={sha256:"06ac115f4c8300049399a6fc6ecff2386262a3e29b108d4e3036f1c17887f090",value:{"id":"b047","title":"橋墩塑鉸韌性設計","titleEn":"Ductile plastic-hinge design for bridge piers","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"從 1989 年賽普勒斯高架橋、1995 年阪神高速神戶線與 1999 年 921 地震的橋墩破壞出發，建立容量設計層級與位移韌性需求，量化圍束箍筋、塑鉸長度與轉角容量，再處理箍筋與續接器施工、反覆載重試驗、震後殘留漂移、塑鉸區腐蝕與既有橋墩的剪力退化評估，說明為何塑鉸只能出現在預先選定、詳細配筋且可檢查的位置。","summaryEn":"Starting from pier failures in the 1989 Cypress Viaduct, the 1995 Hanshin Expressway Kobe Route and the 1999 Chi-Chi earthquake, build the capacity-design hierarchy and displacement-ductility demand, quantify confinement, plastic-hinge length and rotation capacity, then cover hoop and coupler construction, cyclic testing, residual drift, hinge-zone corrosion and shear degradation in existing piers, explaining why plastic hinges may form only at preselected, well-detailed and inspectable locations.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、吊裝或張拉作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, lifting or stressing permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"st-bridge-components-seismic","subcategoryTitle":"支承、伸縮縫與橋梁耐震","subcategoryTitleEn":"Bearings, joints and bridge seismic design","learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-bridge-components-seismic","learningTags":["structures","st-bridge-components-seismic","pier"],"architectureFamily":"pier","architectureNodes":[["地震位移需求","Seismic displacement demand"],["柱塑鉸區（延性保險絲）","Column plastic hinge (ductile fuse)"],["圍束箍筋與主筋","Confining hoops and longitudinal bars"],["能力保護構件（帽梁、基礎、接頭）","Capacity-protected members (cap, footing, joints)"],["反覆載重試驗與模型校驗","Cyclic tests and model calibration"],["震後檢查與既有橋評估","Post-event inspection and existing-pier assessment"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[2,1],[1,3],[4,2],[1,5],[3,5]],"diagram":{"type":"pier","labels":["地震位移需求","柱塑鉸區（延性保險絲）","圍束箍筋與主筋","能力保護構件（帽梁、基礎、接頭）","反覆載重試驗與模型校驗"],"labelsEn":["Seismic displacement demand","Column plastic hinge (ductile fuse)","Confining hoops and longitudinal bars","Capacity-protected members (cap, footing, joints)","Cyclic tests and model calibration"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"設計練習：單柱懸臂圓形橋墩直徑 D = 2.0 m、柱高 L = 10 m、軸力 P = 8 MN，主筋 46 支 36 mm（A_s ≈ 0.0468 m²，ρ_l ≈ 1.5%），f_ye = 475 MPa，以彎矩—曲率分析得 M_p ≈ 12 MN·m（教學假設）。降伏曲率 φ_y ≈ 2.25×0.002375/2.0 ≈ 0.00267 1/m，Δ_y = φ_y·L²/3 ≈ 0.089 m。螺旋筋 22 mm@100 mm，ρ_s = 0.0080，ε_cu ≈ 0.0136，φ_u ≈ 0.0136/0.5 ≈ 0.0272 1/m。L_p = 0.08×10 + 0.022×475×0.036 ≈ 1.18 m，θ_p ≈ (0.0272 − 0.0027)×1.18 ≈ 0.029 rad，Δ_p ≈ 0.029×9.41 ≈ 0.27 m，容量位移 Δ_c ≈ 0.36 m，μ_c ≈ 0.36/0.089 ≈ 4.0（≥ 3）。設計需求 Δ_D = 0.30 m，μ_D ≈ 3.4（≤ 4），Δ_c/Δ_D ≈ 1.2。能力保護：M_o = 1.2×12 = 14.4 MN·m，V_o = 1.44 MN，基礎與柱剪力須以此設計。若螺旋筋間距放寬到 130 mm，ε_cu 降為約 0.0114，Δ_c 降到約 0.31 m，餘裕幾乎消失。數值為教學假設，不代表任何實際橋梁的設計。","textEn":"Design exercise: a single cantilever circular pier with D = 2.0 m, height L = 10 m and axial load P = 8 MN has 46 bars of 36 mm (A_s ≈ 0.0468 m², ρ_l ≈ 1.5%) with f_ye = 475 MPa, and moment–curvature analysis gives M_p ≈ 12 MN·m (teaching assumption). Yield curvature φ_y ≈ 2.25×0.002375/2.0 ≈ 0.00267 1/m and Δ_y = φ_y·L²/3 ≈ 0.089 m. A 22 mm spiral at 100 mm gives ρ_s = 0.0080, ε_cu ≈ 0.0136 and φ_u ≈ 0.0136/0.5 ≈ 0.0272 1/m. L_p = 0.08×10 + 0.022×475×0.036 ≈ 1.18 m, θ_p ≈ (0.0272 − 0.0027)×1.18 ≈ 0.029 rad, Δ_p ≈ 0.029×9.41 ≈ 0.27 m, so capacity Δ_c ≈ 0.36 m and μ_c ≈ 0.36/0.089 ≈ 4.0 (at least 3). With demand Δ_D = 0.30 m, μ_D ≈ 3.4 (at most 4) and Δ_c/Δ_D ≈ 1.2. Capacity protection: M_o = 1.2×12 = 14.4 MN·m and V_o = 1.44 MN govern foundation and column shear design. Widening the spiral pitch to 130 mm lowers ε_cu to about 0.0114 and Δ_c to about 0.31 m, nearly erasing the margin. Values are teaching assumptions, not the design of any real bridge.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":13,"enrichmentVersion":13,"stages":[{"id":"b047-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「容量設計與破壞層級」與「位移需求與韌性限值」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Capacity design and failure hierarchy\" and \"Displacement demand and ductility limits\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b047-v13-01","title":"容量設計與破壞層級：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Capacity design and failure hierarchy: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「超強度彎矩 M_o」如何影響橋墩塑鉸韌性設計的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Overstrength moment M_o” governs force, deformation or durability in “Ductile plastic-hinge design for bridge piers”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"以彈性設計抵抗設計地震對橋墩並不經濟，因此規範允許橋墩以塑性變形消散能量，但必須事先決定「哪裡可以壞、怎麼壞」。容量設計把柱端彎曲塑鉸設為唯一的延性保險絲，其他構件（剪力、帽梁、基礎、梁柱接頭、支承與錨定）都以塑鉸可能達到的超強度彎矩來設計，確保它們保持彈性。這樣即使地震遠超預期，破壞仍以可預測、可修復的彎曲變形出現，而不是脆性剪斷或基礎破壞。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「超強度彎矩 M_o」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Designing piers to stay elastic in the design earthquake is uneconomical, so codes allow piers to dissipate energy by yielding, but the designer must decide in advance where damage may occur and how. Capacity design makes the column-end flexural plastic hinge the only ductile fuse, and designs every other element (shear, cap beam, foundation, beam–column joint, bearings and anchorages) for the overstrength moment the hinge can develop, so that they stay elastic. Even in an earthquake far beyond expectation, damage then appears as predictable, repairable flexural deformation rather than brittle shear or foundation failure. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Overstrength moment M_o” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：超強度彎矩 M_o = 1.2·M_p。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Overstrength moment M_o = 1.2·M_p.","failure":"常見誤解：「橋墩越強越好，所有構件都加強就能確保耐震安全。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The stronger the pier the better; strengthening every member guarantees seismic safety.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「超強度彎矩 M_o」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Overstrength moment M_o”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-01-k1","title":"容量設計與破壞層級","titleEn":"Capacity design and failure hierarchy","text":"以彈性設計抵抗設計地震對橋墩並不經濟，因此規範允許橋墩以塑性變形消散能量，但必須事先決定「哪裡可以壞、怎麼壞」。容量設計把柱端彎曲塑鉸設為唯一的延性保險絲，其他構件（剪力、帽梁、基礎、梁柱接頭、支承與錨定）都以塑鉸可能達到的超強度彎矩來設計，確保它們保持彈性。","textEn":"Designing piers to stay elastic in the design earthquake is uneconomical, so codes allow piers to dissipate energy by yielding, but the designer must decide in advance where damage may occur and how. Capacity design makes the column-end flexural plastic hinge the only ductile fuse, and designs every other element (shear, cap beam, foundation, beam–column joint, bearings and anchorages) for the overstrength moment the hinge can develop, so that they stay elastic.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：橋墩越強越好，所有構件都加強就能確保耐震安全。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The stronger the pier the better; strengthening every member guarantees seismic safety. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「容量設計與破壞層級」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Capacity design and failure hierarchy\" is correct?","options":["橋墩越強越好，所有構件都加強就能確保耐震安全。","以彈性設計抵抗設計地震對橋墩並不經濟，因此規範允許橋墩以塑性變形消散能量，但必須事先決定「哪裡可以壞、怎麼壞」。","只要強度需求以韌性折減後滿足，就不必檢查位移。"],"optionsEn":["The stronger the pier the better; strengthening every member guarantees seismic safety.","Designing piers to stay elastic in the design earthquake is uneconomical, so codes allow piers to dissipate energy by yielding, but the designer must decide in advance where damage may occur and how.","If strength demand reduced by ductility is satisfied, displacement need not be checked."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以彈性設計抵抗設計地震對橋墩並不經濟，因此規範允許橋墩以塑性變形消散能量，但必須事先決定「哪裡可以壞、怎麼壞」。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Designing piers to stay elastic in the design earthquake is uneconomical, so codes allow piers to dissipate energy by yielding, but the designer must decide in advance where damage may occur and how. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b047-v13-02","title":"容量設計與破壞層級：定量估算","titleEn":"Capacity design and failure hierarchy: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「超強度彎矩 M_o」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Overstrength moment M_o” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：超強度彎矩 M_o = 1.2·M_p。M_p = 12 MN·m 時 M_o = 14.4 MN·m；懸臂高 L = 10 m 的單柱，對應剪力 V_o = M_o/L = 1.44 MN，基礎、帽梁與柱剪力都以此設計；若柱高只有 6 m，V_o 升為 2.4 MN。數值為教學假設，係數依所採規範。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Overstrength moment M_o = 1.2·M_p. For M_p = 12 MN·m, M_o = 14.4 MN·m; for a single cantilever column of height L = 10 m the corresponding shear is V_o = M_o/L = 1.44 MN, used to design foundation, cap beam and column shear; a 6 m column raises V_o to 2.4 MN. Values are teaching assumptions; the factor follows the governing code. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以彎矩—曲率分析求得柱的理想化塑性彎矩 M_p（採期望材料強度），乘以超強度係數後，逐一核對柱剪力、帽梁、基礎、樁與接頭的設計強度是否大於對應需求，並在計算書中列出完整的能力保護清單。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Obtain the column's idealised plastic moment M_p from moment–curvature analysis using expected material strengths, apply the overstrength factor, and check that the design strengths of column shear, cap beam, footing, piles and joints exceed the corresponding demands, listing the full capacity-protection table in the calculations.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"超強度彎矩 M_o = 1.2·M_p。M_p = 12 MN·m 時 M_o = 14.4 MN·m；懸臂高 L = 10 m 的單柱，對應剪力 V_o = M_o/L = 1.44 MN，基礎、帽梁與柱剪力都以此設計；若柱高只有 6 m，V_o 升為 2.4 MN。數值為教學假設，係數依所採規範。","textEn":"Overstrength moment M_o = 1.2·M_p. For M_p = 12 MN·m, M_o = 14.4 MN·m; for a single cantilever column of height L = 10 m the corresponding shear is V_o = M_o/L = 1.44 MN, used to design foundation, cap beam and column shear; a 6 m column raises V_o to 2.4 MN. Values are teaching assumptions; the factor follows the governing code.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「容量設計與破壞層級」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Capacity design and failure hierarchy\", which statement holds?","options":["塑鉸長度就是柱底出現裂縫的長度，可以在現場直接量到。","只要續接器能承受鋼筋的降伏強度，就可以用在塑鉸區。","超強度彎矩 M_o = 1.2·M_p。"],"optionsEn":["The plastic-hinge length is simply the cracked length at the column base and can be measured on site.","Any coupler that develops the bar's yield strength can be used in a plastic hinge zone.","Overstrength moment M_o = 1.2·M_p."],"answer":2,"explanation":"超強度彎矩 M_o = 1.2·M_p。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Overstrength moment M_o = 1.2·M_p. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b047-v13-03","title":"容量設計與破壞層級：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Capacity design and failure hierarchy: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「超強度彎矩 M_o」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Overstrength moment M_o” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以彎矩—曲率分析求得柱的理想化塑性彎矩 M_p（採期望材料強度），乘以超強度係數後，逐一核對柱剪力、帽梁、基礎、樁與接頭的設計強度是否大於對應需求，並在計算書中列出完整的能力保護清單。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Obtain the column's idealised plastic moment M_p from moment–curvature analysis using expected material strengths, apply the overstrength factor, and check that the design strengths of column shear, cap beam, footing, piles and joints exceed the corresponding demands, listing the full capacity-protection table in the calculations. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：設計審查時要求一張「延性構件與能力保護構件」對照表，列出塑鉸位置、M_p、M_o 與各能力保護構件的強度比；變更柱配筋時，必須同步重算所有能力保護構件。","observationEn":"Site practice: Design review requires a table of ductile versus capacity-protected members listing hinge locations, M_p, M_o and each protected member's strength ratio; any change to column reinforcement triggers recalculation of all capacity-protected members.","failure":"注意干擾：若剪力或基礎只以設計地震力計算，塑鉸形成前或形成時柱先剪斷，強度在一個循環內驟降；1971 年聖費爾南多與 1989 年洛馬普列塔地震中多座高架橋就因柱剪力與接頭不足而崩塌。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If shear or foundations are designed only for the design earthquake force, the column can fail in shear before or as the hinge forms, losing strength within one cycle; in the 1971 San Fernando and 1989 Loma Prieta earthquakes several viaducts collapsed because of inadequate column shear and joint capacity. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以彎矩—曲率分析求得柱的理想化塑性彎矩 M_p（採期望材料強度），乘以超強度係數後，逐一核對柱剪力、帽梁、基礎、樁與接頭的設計強度是否大於對應需求，並在計算書中列出完整的能力保護清單。","textEn":"Obtain the column's idealised plastic moment M_p from moment–curvature analysis using expected material strengths, apply the overstrength factor, and check that the design strengths of column shear, cap beam, footing, piles and joints exceed the corresponding demands, listing the full capacity-protection table in the calculations.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"設計審查時要求一張「延性構件與能力保護構件」對照表，列出塑鉸位置、M_p、M_o 與各能力保護構件的強度比；變更柱配筋時，必須同步重算所有能力保護構件。","textEn":"Design review requires a table of ductile versus capacity-protected members listing hinge locations, M_p, M_o and each protected member's strength ratio; any change to column reinforcement triggers recalculation of all capacity-protected members.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「容量設計與破壞層級」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Capacity design and failure hierarchy\"?","options":["以彎矩—曲率分析求得柱的理想化塑性彎矩 M_p（採期望材料強度），乘以超強度係數後，逐一核對柱剪力、帽梁、基礎、樁與接頭的設計強度是否大於對應需求，並在計算書中列出完整的能力保護清單。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","震後柱子沒有倒，就表示可以直接恢復通行。"],"optionsEn":["Obtain the column's idealised plastic moment M_p from moment–curvature analysis using expected material strengths, apply the overstrength factor, and check that the design strengths of column shear, cap beam, footing, piles and joints exceed the corresponding demands, listing the full capacity-protection table in the calculations.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","If a column did not collapse in the earthquake, the bridge can reopen immediately."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以彎矩—曲率分析求得柱的理想化塑性彎矩 M_p（採期望材料強度），乘以超強度係數後，逐一核對柱剪力、帽梁、基礎、樁與接頭的設計強度是否大於對應需求，並在計算書中列出完整的能力保護清單。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Obtain the column's idealised plastic moment M_p from moment–curvature analysis using expected material strengths, apply the overstrength factor, and check that the design strengths of column shear, cap beam, footing, piles and joints exceed the corresponding demands, listing the full capacity-protection table in the calculations. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b047-v13-04","title":"容量設計與破壞層級：失效診斷","titleEn":"Capacity design and failure hierarchy: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「超強度彎矩 M_o」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Overstrength moment M_o” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若剪力或基礎只以設計地震力計算，塑鉸形成前或形成時柱先剪斷，強度在一個循環內驟降；1971 年聖費爾南多與 1989 年洛馬普列塔地震中多座高架橋就因柱剪力與接頭不足而崩塌。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If shear or foundations are designed only for the design earthquake force, the column can fail in shear before or as the hinge forms, losing strength within one cycle; in the 1971 San Fernando and 1989 Loma Prieta earthquakes several viaducts collapsed because of inadequate column shear and joint capacity. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這樣即使地震遠超預期，破壞仍以可預測、可修復的彎曲變形出現，而不是脆性剪斷或基礎破壞。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Even in an earthquake far beyond expectation, damage then appears as predictable, repairable flexural deformation rather than brittle shear or foundation failure.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「橋墩越強越好，所有構件都加強就能確保耐震安全。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The stronger the pier the better; strengthening every member guarantees seismic safety.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若剪力或基礎只以設計地震力計算，塑鉸形成前或形成時柱先剪斷，強度在一個循環內驟降；1971 年聖費爾南多與 1989 年洛馬普列塔地震中多座高架橋就因柱剪力與接頭不足而崩塌。","textEn":"If shear or foundations are designed only for the design earthquake force, the column can fail in shear before or as the hinge forms, losing strength within one cycle; in the 1971 San Fernando and 1989 Loma Prieta earthquakes several viaducts collapsed because of inadequate column shear and joint capacity.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「容量設計與破壞層級」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Capacity design and failure hierarchy\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若剪力或基礎只以設計地震力計算，塑鉸形成前或形成時柱先剪斷，強度在一個循環內驟降。","只要強度需求以韌性折減後滿足，就不必檢查位移。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","If shear or foundations are designed only for the design earthquake force, the column can fail in shear before or as the hinge forms, losing strength within one cycle.","If strength demand reduced by ductility is satisfied, displacement need not be checked."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若剪力或基礎只以設計地震力計算，塑鉸形成前或形成時柱先剪斷，強度在一個循環內驟降；1971 年聖費爾南多與 1989 年洛馬普列塔地震中多座高架橋就因柱剪力與接頭不足而崩塌。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If shear or foundations are designed only for the design earthquake force, the column can fail in shear before or as the hinge forms, losing strength within one cycle; in the 1971 San Fernando and 1989 Loma Prieta earthquakes several viaducts collapsed because of inadequate column shear and joint capacity. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b047-v13-05","title":"位移需求與韌性限值：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Displacement demand and ductility limits: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「位移韌性需求 μ_D」如何影響橋墩塑鉸韌性設計的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Displacement ductility demand μ_D” governs force, deformation or durability in “Ductile plastic-hinge design for bridge piers”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"對週期較長的橋梁，等位移原則指出非線性結構的最大位移與同週期的彈性結構相近，因此設計可先求彈性位移需求，再除以柱的降伏位移得到位移韌性需求 μ_D。韌性需求越高，塑鉸轉角越大、損傷越重；加州運輸局耐震設計準則 1.7 版把固定基礎單柱橋墩的 μ_D 限制在 4、多柱排架限制在 5，並要求每個延性構件的局部位移韌性容量至少為 3。限值的目的是讓需求與容量之間保有餘裕，同時把震後損傷控制在可修復範圍。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「位移韌性需求 μ_D」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"For longer-period bridges the equal-displacement principle says the peak displacement of a nonlinear structure is close to that of an elastic structure with the same period, so design first finds the elastic displacement demand and divides it by the column's yield displacement to get the displacement ductility demand μ_D. Higher demand means larger hinge rotations and heavier damage; Caltrans Seismic Design Criteria version 1.7 limits μ_D to 4 for single-column bents on fixed foundations and 5 for multi-column bents, and requires each ductile member to have a local displacement ductility capacity of at least 3. The limits keep a margin between demand and capacity and hold post-earthquake damage within a repairable range. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Displacement ductility demand μ_D” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：降伏曲率 φ_y ≈ 2.25·ε_y/D，ε_y = 475/200,000 = 0.002375，D = 2.0 m，φ_y ≈ 0.00267 1/m；降伏位移 Δ_y = φ_y·L²/3 = 0.00267×10²/3 ≈ 0.089 m（未計鋼筋滑移）。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Yield curvature φ_y ≈ 2.25·ε_y/D with ε_y = 475/200,000 = 0.002375 and D = 2.0 m gives φ_y ≈ 0.00267 1/m; yield displacement Δ_y = φ_y·L²/3 = 0.00267×10²/3 ≈ 0.089 m, ignoring bar slip.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要強度需求以韌性折減後滿足，就不必檢查位移。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If strength demand reduced by ductility is satisfied, displacement need not be checked.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「位移韌性需求 μ_D」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Displacement ductility demand μ_D”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-05-k1","title":"位移需求與韌性限值","titleEn":"Displacement demand and ductility limits","text":"對週期較長的橋梁，等位移原則指出非線性結構的最大位移與同週期的彈性結構相近，因此設計可先求彈性位移需求，再除以柱的降伏位移得到位移韌性需求 μ_D。韌性需求越高，塑鉸轉角越大、損傷越重；加州運輸局耐震設計準則 1.7 版把固定基礎單柱橋墩的 μ_D 限制在 4、多柱排架限制在 5，並要求每個延性構件的局部位移韌性容量至少為 3。","textEn":"For longer-period bridges the equal-displacement principle says the peak displacement of a nonlinear structure is close to that of an elastic structure with the same period, so design first finds the elastic displacement demand and divides it by the column's yield displacement to get the displacement ductility demand μ_D. Higher demand means larger hinge rotations and heavier damage; Caltrans Seismic Design Criteria version 1.7 limits μ_D to 4 for single-column bents on fixed foundations and 5 for multi-column bents, and requires each ductile member to have a local displacement ductility capacity of at least 3.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要強度需求以韌性折減後滿足，就不必檢查位移。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If strength demand reduced by ductility is satisfied, displacement need not be checked. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「位移需求與韌性限值」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Displacement demand and ductility limits\" is correct?","options":["只要強度需求以韌性折減後滿足，就不必檢查位移。","箍筋主要是用來固定主筋位置，對耐震性能影響不大。","對週期較長的橋梁，等位移原則指出非線性結構的最大位移與同週期的彈性結構相近，因此設計可先求彈性位移需求，再除以柱的降伏位移得到位移韌性需求 μ_D。"],"optionsEn":["If strength demand reduced by ductility is satisfied, displacement need not be checked.","Hoops mainly hold the longitudinal bars in place and matter little for seismic performance.","For longer-period bridges the equal-displacement principle says the peak displacement of a nonlinear structure is close to that of an elastic structure with the same period, so design first finds the elastic displacement demand and divides it by the column's yield displacement to get the displacement ductility demand μ_D."],"answer":2,"explanation":"對週期較長的橋梁，等位移原則指出非線性結構的最大位移與同週期的彈性結構相近，因此設計可先求彈性位移需求，再除以柱的降伏位移得到位移韌性需求 μ_D。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"For longer-period bridges the equal-displacement principle says the peak displacement of a nonlinear structure is close to that of an elastic structure with the same period, so design first finds the elastic displacement demand and divides it by the column's yield displacement to get the displacement ductility demand μ_D. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b047-v13-06","title":"位移需求與韌性限值：定量估算","titleEn":"Displacement demand and ductility limits: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「位移韌性需求 μ_D」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Displacement ductility demand μ_D” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：降伏曲率 φ_y ≈ 2.25·ε_y/D，ε_y = 475/200,000 = 0.002375，D = 2.0 m，φ_y ≈ 0.00267 1/m；降伏位移 Δ_y = φ_y·L²/3 = 0.00267×10²/3 ≈ 0.089 m（未計鋼筋滑移）。彈性位移需求 Δ_D = 0.30 m，μ_D = 0.30/0.089 ≈ 3.4，小於 4。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Yield curvature φ_y ≈ 2.25·ε_y/D with ε_y = 475/200,000 = 0.002375 and D = 2.0 m gives φ_y ≈ 0.00267 1/m; yield displacement Δ_y = φ_y·L²/3 = 0.00267×10²/3 ≈ 0.089 m, ignoring bar slip. For an elastic displacement demand Δ_D = 0.30 m, μ_D = 0.30/0.089 ≈ 3.4, below 4. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以反應譜或非線性時間歷程分析求得每座排架的位移需求，與推覆分析（pushover）得到的降伏位移與容量位移比較，確認 μ_D 不超過規範限值且 Δ_D 小於容量位移；短週期橋梁要另加位移放大係數。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Obtain each bent's displacement demand by response-spectrum or nonlinear time-history analysis and compare it with yield and capacity displacements from pushover analysis, confirming μ_D stays within the code limit and Δ_D below capacity; short-period bridges need an additional displacement magnification factor.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"降伏曲率 φ_y ≈ 2.25·ε_y/D，ε_y = 475/200,000 = 0.002375，D = 2.0 m，φ_y ≈ 0.00267 1/m；降伏位移 Δ_y = φ_y·L²/3 = 0.00267×10²/3 ≈ 0.089 m（未計鋼筋滑移）。彈性位移需求 Δ_D = 0.30 m，μ_D = 0.30/0.089 ≈ 3.4，小於 4。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Yield curvature φ_y ≈ 2.25·ε_y/D with ε_y = 475/200,000 = 0.002375 and D = 2.0 m gives φ_y ≈ 0.00267 1/m; yield displacement Δ_y = φ_y·L²/3 = 0.00267×10²/3 ≈ 0.089 m, ignoring bar slip. For an elastic displacement demand Δ_D = 0.30 m, μ_D = 0.30/0.089 ≈ 3.4, below 4. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「位移需求與韌性限值」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Displacement demand and ductility limits\", which statement holds?","options":["降伏曲率 φ_y ≈ 2.25·ε_y/D，ε_y = 475/200,000 = 0.002375，D = 2.0 m，φ_y ≈ 0.00267 1/m。","箍筋間距差幾公分不影響結構安全，可以依現場方便調整。","單調推到破壞的試驗就足以代表地震下的柱韌性。"],"optionsEn":["Yield curvature φ_y ≈ 2.25·ε_y/D with ε_y = 475/200,000 = 0.002375 and D = 2.0 m gives φ_y ≈ 0.00267 1/m.","A few centimetres of extra hoop spacing do not affect safety and can be adjusted for site convenience.","A monotonic push to failure is enough to represent column ductility under earthquakes."],"answer":0,"explanation":"降伏曲率 φ_y ≈ 2.25·ε_y/D，ε_y = 475/200,000 = 0.002375，D = 2.0 m，φ_y ≈ 0.00267 1/m；降伏位移 Δ_y = φ_y·L²/3 = 0.00267×10²/3 ≈ 0.089 m（未計鋼筋滑移）。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Yield curvature φ_y ≈ 2.25·ε_y/D with ε_y = 475/200,000 = 0.002375 and D = 2.0 m gives φ_y ≈ 0.00267 1/m; yield displacement Δ_y = φ_y·L²/3 = 0.00267×10²/3 ≈ 0.089 m, ignoring bar slip. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b047-v13-07","title":"位移需求與韌性限值：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Displacement demand and ductility limits: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「位移韌性需求 μ_D」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Displacement ductility demand μ_D” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以反應譜或非線性時間歷程分析求得每座排架的位移需求，與推覆分析（pushover）得到的降伏位移與容量位移比較，確認 μ_D 不超過規範限值且 Δ_D 小於容量位移；短週期橋梁要另加位移放大係數。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Obtain each bent's displacement demand by response-spectrum or nonlinear time-history analysis and compare it with yield and capacity displacements from pushover analysis, confirming μ_D stays within the code limit and Δ_D below capacity; short-period bridges need an additional displacement magnification factor. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：相鄰排架的有效勁度比應盡量接近（例如以墩高、斷面或基礎埋深調整），設計報告須列出每座排架的 Δ_D、Δ_y、Δ_c 與 μ_D，作為審查與後續評估的基準。","observationEn":"Site practice: Keep effective stiffness ratios of adjacent bents close, adjusting pier height, section or foundation embedment, and list Δ_D, Δ_y, Δ_c and μ_D for every bent in the design report as the baseline for review and later assessment.","failure":"注意干擾：同一座橋中長短不一的橋墩若未調整勁度，短墩吸收大部分地震力且韌性需求集中，可能先達到剪力或韌性極限；忽略短週期放大則低估位移，使塑鉸轉角超過容量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If piers of very different heights in one bridge are not balanced in stiffness, the short piers attract most of the seismic force and concentrate ductility demand, reaching shear or ductility limits first; ignoring short-period magnification underestimates displacement and drives hinge rotation beyond capacity. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以反應譜或非線性時間歷程分析求得每座排架的位移需求，與推覆分析（pushover）得到的降伏位移與容量位移比較，確認 μ_D 不超過規範限值且 Δ_D 小於容量位移；短週期橋梁要另加位移放大係數。","textEn":"Obtain each bent's displacement demand by response-spectrum or nonlinear time-history analysis and compare it with yield and capacity displacements from pushover analysis, confirming μ_D stays within the code limit and Δ_D below capacity; short-period bridges need an additional displacement magnification factor.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"相鄰排架的有效勁度比應盡量接近（例如以墩高、斷面或基礎埋深調整），設計報告須列出每座排架的 Δ_D、Δ_y、Δ_c 與 μ_D，作為審查與後續評估的基準。","textEn":"Keep effective stiffness ratios of adjacent bents close, adjusting pier height, section or foundation embedment, and list Δ_D, Δ_y, Δ_c and μ_D for every bent in the design report as the baseline for review and later assessment.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「位移需求與韌性限值」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Displacement demand and ductility limits\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以反應譜或非線性時間歷程分析求得每座排架的位移需求，與推覆分析（pushover）得到的降伏位移與容量位移比較，確認 μ_D 不超過規範限值且 Δ_D 小於容量位移。","耐震與耐久是兩個獨立問題，腐蝕不會影響橋墩的耐震能力。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Obtain each bent's displacement demand by response-spectrum or nonlinear time-history analysis and compare it with yield and capacity displacements from pushover analysis, confirming μ_D stays within the code limit and Δ_D below capacity.","Seismic and durability performance are separate issues; corrosion does not affect a pier's seismic capacity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以反應譜或非線性時間歷程分析求得每座排架的位移需求，與推覆分析（pushover）得到的降伏位移與容量位移比較，確認 μ_D 不超過規範限值且 Δ_D 小於容量位移；短週期橋梁要另加位移放大係數。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Obtain each bent's displacement demand by response-spectrum or nonlinear time-history analysis and compare it with yield and capacity displacements from pushover analysis, confirming μ_D stays within the code limit and Δ_D below capacity; short-period bridges need an additional displacement magnification factor. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b047-v13-08","title":"位移需求與韌性限值：失效診斷","titleEn":"Displacement demand and ductility limits: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「位移韌性需求 μ_D」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Displacement ductility demand μ_D” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"同一座橋中長短不一的橋墩若未調整勁度，短墩吸收大部分地震力且韌性需求集中，可能先達到剪力或韌性極限；忽略短週期放大則低估位移，使塑鉸轉角超過容量。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If piers of very different heights in one bridge are not balanced in stiffness, the short piers attract most of the seismic force and concentrate ductility demand, reaching shear or ductility limits first; ignoring short-period magnification underestimates displacement and drives hinge rotation beyond capacity. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：限值的目的是讓需求與容量之間保有餘裕，同時把震後損傷控制在可修復範圍。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The limits keep a margin between demand and capacity and hold post-earthquake damage within a repairable range.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要強度需求以韌性折減後滿足，就不必檢查位移。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If strength demand reduced by ductility is satisfied, displacement need not be checked.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"同一座橋中長短不一的橋墩若未調整勁度，短墩吸收大部分地震力且韌性需求集中，可能先達到剪力或韌性極限；忽略短週期放大則低估位移，使塑鉸轉角超過容量。","textEn":"If piers of very different heights in one bridge are not balanced in stiffness, the short piers attract most of the seismic force and concentrate ductility demand, reaching shear or ductility limits first; ignoring short-period magnification underestimates displacement and drives hinge rotation beyond capacity.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「位移需求與韌性限值」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Displacement demand and ductility limits\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","箍筋主要是用來固定主筋位置，對耐震性能影響不大。","同一座橋中長短不一的橋墩若未調整勁度，短墩吸收大部分地震力且韌性需求集中，可能先達到剪力或韌性極限；忽略短週期放大則低估位移，使塑鉸轉角超過容量。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Hoops mainly hold the longitudinal bars in place and matter little for seismic performance.","If piers of very different heights in one bridge are not balanced in stiffness, the short piers attract most of the seismic force and concentrate ductility demand, reaching shear or ductility limits first."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同一座橋中長短不一的橋墩若未調整勁度，短墩吸收大部分地震力且韌性需求集中，可能先達到剪力或韌性極限；忽略短週期放大則低估位移，使塑鉸轉角超過容量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If piers of very different heights in one bridge are not balanced in stiffness, the short piers attract most of the seismic force and concentrate ductility demand, reaching shear or ductility limits first; ignoring short-period magnification underestimates displacement and drives hinge rotation beyond capacity. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b047-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「圍束箍筋與核心混凝土」與「塑鉸長度、轉角容量與搭接禁區」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Confining hoops and core concrete\" and \"Hinge length, rotation capacity and no-splice zones\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b047-v13-09","title":"圍束箍筋與核心混凝土：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Confining hoops and core concrete: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「螺旋箍筋體積比 ρ_s」如何影響橋墩塑鉸韌性設計的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Spiral volumetric ratio ρ_s” governs force, deformation or durability in “Ductile plastic-hinge design for bridge piers”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"塑鉸轉角容量主要取決於受壓區混凝土能承受多大壓應變：保護層混凝土在應變約 0.004 時剝落，但被螺旋箍筋或封閉箍筋圍束的核心混凝土，受到箍筋的側向反力，強度與極限應變都大幅提高。圍束同時防止縱向主筋在反覆載重下挫屈，以及提供剪力強度。圓形斷面用螺旋筋圍束效率最高，矩形斷面則需要繫筋把箍筋的長邊拉住，否則箍筋向外彎曲，圍束作用只在角落有效。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「螺旋箍筋體積比 ρ_s」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The rotation capacity of a plastic hinge depends mainly on how much compressive strain the concrete can sustain: cover concrete spalls at a strain of about 0.004, but core concrete confined by spirals or closed hoops gains strength and ultimate strain from the hoops' lateral reaction. Confinement also stops longitudinal bars buckling under reversed loading and supplies shear strength. Circular sections confined by spirals are the most efficient; rectangular sections need cross-ties to restrain the long sides of the hoops, or the hoops bow outward and confine effectively only at the corners. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Spiral volumetric ratio ρ_s” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：ρ_s = 4·A_sp/(D′·s)，22 mm 螺旋筋 A_sp = 380 mm²、核心直徑 D′ = 1,900 mm、間距 s = 100 mm，ρ_s = 1,520/190,000 = 0.0080。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: ρ_s = 4·A_sp/(D′·s); a 22 mm spiral with A_sp = 380 mm², core diameter D′ = 1,900 mm and pitch s = 100 mm gives ρ_s = 1,520/190,000 = 0.0080.","failure":"常見誤解：「箍筋主要是用來固定主筋位置，對耐震性能影響不大。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Hoops mainly hold the longitudinal bars in place and matter little for seismic performance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「螺旋箍筋體積比 ρ_s」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Spiral volumetric ratio ρ_s”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-09-k1","title":"圍束箍筋與核心混凝土","titleEn":"Confining hoops and core concrete","text":"塑鉸轉角容量主要取決於受壓區混凝土能承受多大壓應變：保護層混凝土在應變約 0.004 時剝落，但被螺旋箍筋或封閉箍筋圍束的核心混凝土，受到箍筋的側向反力，強度與極限應變都大幅提高。圍束同時防止縱向主筋在反覆載重下挫屈，以及提供剪力強度。","textEn":"The rotation capacity of a plastic hinge depends mainly on how much compressive strain the concrete can sustain: cover concrete spalls at a strain of about 0.004, but core concrete confined by spirals or closed hoops gains strength and ultimate strain from the hoops' lateral reaction. Confinement also stops longitudinal bars buckling under reversed loading and supplies shear strength.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：箍筋主要是用來固定主筋位置，對耐震性能影響不大。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Hoops mainly hold the longitudinal bars in place and matter little for seismic performance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「圍束箍筋與核心混凝土」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Confining hoops and core concrete\" is correct?","options":["塑鉸轉角容量主要取決於受壓區混凝土能承受多大壓應變：保護層混凝土在應變約 0.004 時剝落，但被螺旋箍筋或封閉箍筋圍束的核心混凝土，受到箍筋的側向反力，強度與極限應變都大幅提高。","箍筋主要是用來固定主筋位置，對耐震性能影響不大。","塑鉸長度就是柱底出現裂縫的長度，可以在現場直接量到。"],"optionsEn":["The rotation capacity of a plastic hinge depends mainly on how much compressive strain the concrete can sustain: cover concrete spalls at a strain of about 0.004, but core concrete confined by spirals or closed hoops gains strength and ultimate strain from the hoops' lateral reaction.","Hoops mainly hold the longitudinal bars in place and matter little for seismic performance.","The plastic-hinge length is simply the cracked length at the column base and can be measured on site."],"answer":0,"explanation":"塑鉸轉角容量主要取決於受壓區混凝土能承受多大壓應變：保護層混凝土在應變約 0.004 時剝落，但被螺旋箍筋或封閉箍筋圍束的核心混凝土，受到箍筋的側向反力，強度與極限應變都大幅提高。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The rotation capacity of a plastic hinge depends mainly on how much compressive strain the concrete can sustain: cover concrete spalls at a strain of about 0.004, but core concrete confined by spirals or closed hoops gains strength and ultimate strain from the hoops' lateral reaction. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b047-v13-10","title":"圍束箍筋與核心混凝土：定量估算","titleEn":"Confining hoops and core concrete: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「螺旋箍筋體積比 ρ_s」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Spiral volumetric ratio ρ_s” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：ρ_s = 4·A_sp/(D′·s)，22 mm 螺旋筋 A_sp = 380 mm²、核心直徑 D′ = 1,900 mm、間距 s = 100 mm，ρ_s = 1,520/190,000 = 0.0080。極限應變 ε_cu = 0.004 + 1.4·ρ_s·f_yh·ε_su/f′_cc = 0.004 + 1.4×0.008×475×0.09/50 ≈ 0.0136，約為未圍束值的 3.4 倍。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: ρ_s = 4·A_sp/(D′·s); a 22 mm spiral with A_sp = 380 mm², core diameter D′ = 1,900 mm and pitch s = 100 mm gives ρ_s = 1,520/190,000 = 0.0080. Ultimate strain ε_cu = 0.004 + 1.4·ρ_s·f_yh·ε_su/f′_cc = 0.004 + 1.4×0.008×475×0.09/50 ≈ 0.0136, about 3.4 times the unconfined value. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以 Mander 等圍束混凝土模型建立彎矩—曲率分析，確認極限曲率由核心混凝土壓應變或主筋拉應變控制；並檢查箍筋間距不超過規範對防止主筋挫屈的上限（常以主筋直徑的倍數表示）。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build the moment–curvature analysis with a confined-concrete model such as Mander's, confirming whether ultimate curvature is governed by core compressive strain or bar tensile strain; check that hoop spacing does not exceed the code limit for preventing bar buckling, usually expressed as a multiple of bar diameter.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"ρ_s = 4·A_sp/(D′·s)，22 mm 螺旋筋 A_sp = 380 mm²、核心直徑 D′ = 1,900 mm、間距 s = 100 mm，ρ_s = 1,520/190,000 = 0.0080。極限應變 ε_cu = 0.004 + 1.4·ρ_s·f_yh·ε_su/f′_cc = 0.004 + 1.4×0.008×475×0.09/50 ≈ 0.0136，約為未圍束值的 3.4 倍。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"ρ_s = 4·A_sp/(D′·s); a 22 mm spiral with A_sp = 380 mm², core diameter D′ = 1,900 mm and pitch s = 100 mm gives ρ_s = 1,520/190,000 = 0.0080. Ultimate strain ε_cu = 0.004 + 1.4·ρ_s·f_yh·ε_su/f′_cc = 0.004 + 1.4×0.008×475×0.09/50 ≈ 0.0136, about 3.4 times the unconfined value. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「圍束箍筋與核心混凝土」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Confining hoops and core concrete\", which statement holds?","options":["只要續接器能承受鋼筋的降伏強度，就可以用在塑鉸區。","ρ_s = 4·A_sp/(D′·s)，22 mm 螺旋筋 A_sp = 380 mm²、核心直徑 D′ = 1,900 mm、間距 s = 100 mm，ρ_s = 1,520/190,000 = 0.0080。","震後柱子沒有倒，就表示可以直接恢復通行。"],"optionsEn":["Any coupler that develops the bar's yield strength can be used in a plastic hinge zone.","ρ_s = 4·A_sp/(D′·s); a 22 mm spiral with A_sp = 380 mm², core diameter D′ = 1,900 mm and pitch s = 100 mm gives ρ_s = 1,520/190,000 = 0.0080.","If a column did not collapse in the earthquake, the bridge can reopen immediately."],"answer":1,"explanation":"ρ_s = 4·A_sp/(D′·s)，22 mm 螺旋筋 A_sp = 380 mm²、核心直徑 D′ = 1,900 mm、間距 s = 100 mm，ρ_s = 1,520/190,000 = 0.0080。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"ρ_s = 4·A_sp/(D′·s); a 22 mm spiral with A_sp = 380 mm², core diameter D′ = 1,900 mm and pitch s = 100 mm gives ρ_s = 1,520/190,000 = 0.0080. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b047-v13-11","title":"圍束箍筋與核心混凝土：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Confining hoops and core concrete: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「螺旋箍筋體積比 ρ_s」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Spiral volumetric ratio ρ_s” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以 Mander 等圍束混凝土模型建立彎矩—曲率分析，確認極限曲率由核心混凝土壓應變或主筋拉應變控制；並檢查箍筋間距不超過規範對防止主筋挫屈的上限（常以主筋直徑的倍數表示）。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build the moment–curvature analysis with a confined-concrete model such as Mander's, confirming whether ultimate curvature is governed by core compressive strain or bar tensile strain; check that hoop spacing does not exceed the code limit for preventing bar buckling, usually expressed as a multiple of bar diameter. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：塑鉸區的箍筋必須是封閉箍或連續螺旋，彎鉤以 135 度彎入核心並有足夠延伸長度，或採焊接封閉箍；圖面要單獨繪出塑鉸區的箍筋間距與範圍，不得以一般區配筋替代。","observationEn":"Site practice: Hinge-zone hoops must be closed hoops or continuous spirals, with 135-degree hooks anchored into the core with adequate extension, or welded closed hoops; drawings show hinge-zone spacing and extent separately and must not substitute general-zone detailing.","failure":"注意干擾：1989 年洛馬普列塔地震中崩塌的賽普勒斯街高架橋，柱缺乏足夠的環向圍束以防止爆裂，上下柱之間也缺少鋼筋連接；圍束不足的柱在保護層剝落後核心壓碎、主筋外凸挫屈，強度與軸向承載同時喪失。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: The Cypress Street Viaduct, which collapsed in the 1989 Loma Prieta earthquake, had columns lacking enough hoop confinement to prevent bursting and upper columns not tied to the lower ones with reinforcement; in poorly confined columns, once the cover spalls the core crushes and bars buckle outward, losing both lateral strength and axial capacity. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以 Mander 等圍束混凝土模型建立彎矩—曲率分析，確認極限曲率由核心混凝土壓應變或主筋拉應變控制；並檢查箍筋間距不超過規範對防止主筋挫屈的上限（常以主筋直徑的倍數表示）。","textEn":"Build the moment–curvature analysis with a confined-concrete model such as Mander's, confirming whether ultimate curvature is governed by core compressive strain or bar tensile strain; check that hoop spacing does not exceed the code limit for preventing bar buckling, usually expressed as a multiple of bar diameter.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"塑鉸區的箍筋必須是封閉箍或連續螺旋，彎鉤以 135 度彎入核心並有足夠延伸長度，或採焊接封閉箍；圖面要單獨繪出塑鉸區的箍筋間距與範圍，不得以一般區配筋替代。","textEn":"Hinge-zone hoops must be closed hoops or continuous spirals, with 135-degree hooks anchored into the core with adequate extension, or welded closed hoops; drawings show hinge-zone spacing and extent separately and must not substitute general-zone detailing.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「圍束箍筋與核心混凝土」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Confining hoops and core concrete\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","混凝土剪力強度是固定值，不會因柱子的彎曲變形而改變。","以 Mander 等圍束混凝土模型建立彎矩—曲率分析，確認極限曲率由核心混凝土壓應變或主筋拉應變控制。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","The concrete shear strength is a fixed value that does not change with column flexural deformation.","Build the moment–curvature analysis with a confined-concrete model such as Mander's, confirming whether ultimate curvature is governed by core compressive strain or bar tensile strain."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以 Mander 等圍束混凝土模型建立彎矩—曲率分析，確認極限曲率由核心混凝土壓應變或主筋拉應變控制；並檢查箍筋間距不超過規範對防止主筋挫屈的上限（常以主筋直徑的倍數表示）。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build the moment–curvature analysis with a confined-concrete model such as Mander's, confirming whether ultimate curvature is governed by core compressive strain or bar tensile strain; check that hoop spacing does not exceed the code limit for preventing bar buckling, usually expressed as a multiple of bar diameter. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b047-v13-12","title":"圍束箍筋與核心混凝土：失效診斷","titleEn":"Confining hoops and core concrete: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「螺旋箍筋體積比 ρ_s」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Spiral volumetric ratio ρ_s” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"1989 年洛馬普列塔地震中崩塌的賽普勒斯街高架橋，柱缺乏足夠的環向圍束以防止爆裂，上下柱之間也缺少鋼筋連接；圍束不足的柱在保護層剝落後核心壓碎、主筋外凸挫屈，強度與軸向承載同時喪失。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"The Cypress Street Viaduct, which collapsed in the 1989 Loma Prieta earthquake, had columns lacking enough hoop confinement to prevent bursting and upper columns not tied to the lower ones with reinforcement; in poorly confined columns, once the cover spalls the core crushes and bars buckle outward, losing both lateral strength and axial capacity. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：圓形斷面用螺旋筋圍束效率最高，矩形斷面則需要繫筋把箍筋的長邊拉住，否則箍筋向外彎曲，圍束作用只在角落有效。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Circular sections confined by spirals are the most efficient; rectangular sections need cross-ties to restrain the long sides of the hoops, or the hoops bow outward and confine effectively only at the corners.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「箍筋主要是用來固定主筋位置，對耐震性能影響不大。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Hoops mainly hold the longitudinal bars in place and matter little for seismic performance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"1989 年洛馬普列塔地震中崩塌的賽普勒斯街高架橋，柱缺乏足夠的環向圍束以防止爆裂，上下柱之間也缺少鋼筋連接；圍束不足的柱在保護層剝落後核心壓碎、主筋外凸挫屈，強度與軸向承載同時喪失。","textEn":"The Cypress Street Viaduct, which collapsed in the 1989 Loma Prieta earthquake, had columns lacking enough hoop confinement to prevent bursting and upper columns not tied to the lower ones with reinforcement; in poorly confined columns, once the cover spalls the core crushes and bars buckle outward, losing both lateral strength and axial capacity.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「圍束箍筋與核心混凝土」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Confining hoops and core concrete\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["1989 年洛馬普列塔地震中崩塌的賽普勒斯街高架橋，柱缺乏足夠的環向圍束以防止爆裂，上下柱之間也缺少鋼筋連接。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","塑鉸長度就是柱底出現裂縫的長度，可以在現場直接量到。"],"optionsEn":["The Cypress Street Viaduct, which collapsed in the 1989 Loma Prieta earthquake, had columns lacking enough hoop confinement to prevent bursting and upper columns not tied to the lower ones with reinforcement.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","The plastic-hinge length is simply the cracked length at the column base and can be measured on site."],"answer":0,"explanation":"1989 年洛馬普列塔地震中崩塌的賽普勒斯街高架橋，柱缺乏足夠的環向圍束以防止爆裂，上下柱之間也缺少鋼筋連接；圍束不足的柱在保護層剝落後核心壓碎、主筋外凸挫屈，強度與軸向承載同時喪失。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"The Cypress Street Viaduct, which collapsed in the 1989 Loma Prieta earthquake, had columns lacking enough hoop confinement to prevent bursting and upper columns not tied to the lower ones with reinforcement; in poorly confined columns, once the cover spalls the core crushes and bars buckle outward, losing both lateral strength and axial capacity. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b047-v13-13","title":"塑鉸長度、轉角容量與搭接禁區：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Hinge length, rotation capacity and no-splice zones: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「塑鉸長度 L_p」如何影響橋墩塑鉸韌性設計的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Plastic-hinge length L_p” governs force, deformation or durability in “Ductile plastic-hinge design for bridge piers”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"實際塑性變形分布在柱底一段區域內，為了計算方便，以等效塑鉸長度 L_p 把曲率集中成一個轉角：L_p 一部分來自柱高（彎矩梯度），一部分來自主筋在基礎中的應變滲透，因此與主筋直徑及降伏強度有關。塑鉸轉角容量等於（極限曲率 − 降伏曲率）乘以 L_p，再乘以柱高換算為塑性位移。塑鉸區內不允許主筋搭接，因為搭接在反覆大應變下會滑脫，這正是許多早期橋墩在柱底搭接處破壞的原因。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「塑鉸長度 L_p」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Plastic deformation actually spreads over a zone at the column base; for convenience an equivalent plastic-hinge length L_p concentrates curvature into one rotation. Part of L_p comes from the column height through moment gradient and part from strain penetration of the bars into the footing, so it depends on bar diameter and yield strength. Hinge rotation capacity equals ultimate minus yield curvature times L_p, converted to plastic displacement through the column height. Lap splices are not allowed in the hinge zone because they slip under reversed large strains, which is why many older piers failed at base lap splices. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Plastic-hinge length L_p” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：等效塑鉸長度 L_p = 0.08·L + 0.022·f_ye·d_bl = 0.08×10 + 0.022×475×0.036 ≈ 1.18 m（不小於 0.044·f_ye·d_bl ≈ 0.75 m）。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: L_p = 0.08·L + 0.022·f_ye·d_bl = 0.08×10 + 0.022×475×0.036 ≈ 1.18 m (not less than 0.044·f_ye·d_bl ≈ 0.75 m).","failure":"常見誤解：「塑鉸長度就是柱底出現裂縫的長度，可以在現場直接量到。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The plastic-hinge length is simply the cracked length at the column base and can be measured on site.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「塑鉸長度 L_p」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Plastic-hinge length L_p”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-13-k1","title":"塑鉸長度、轉角容量與搭接禁區","titleEn":"Hinge length, rotation capacity and no-splice zones","text":"實際塑性變形分布在柱底一段區域內，為了計算方便，以等效塑鉸長度 L_p 把曲率集中成一個轉角：L_p 一部分來自柱高（彎矩梯度），一部分來自主筋在基礎中的應變滲透，因此與主筋直徑及降伏強度有關。塑鉸轉角容量等於（極限曲率 − 降伏曲率）乘以 L_p，再乘以柱高換算為塑性位移。","textEn":"Plastic deformation actually spreads over a zone at the column base; for convenience an equivalent plastic-hinge length L_p concentrates curvature into one rotation. Part of L_p comes from the column height through moment gradient and part from strain penetration of the bars into the footing, so it depends on bar diameter and yield strength.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：塑鉸長度就是柱底出現裂縫的長度，可以在現場直接量到。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The plastic-hinge length is simply the cracked length at the column base and can be measured on site. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「塑鉸長度、轉角容量與搭接禁區」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Hinge length, rotation capacity and no-splice zones\" is correct?","options":["塑鉸長度就是柱底出現裂縫的長度，可以在現場直接量到。","實際塑性變形分布在柱底一段區域內，為了計算方便，以等效塑鉸長度 L_p 把曲率集中成一個轉角：L_p 一部分來自柱高（彎矩梯度），一部分來自主筋在基礎中的應變滲透，因此與主筋直徑及降伏強度有關。","箍筋間距差幾公分不影響結構安全，可以依現場方便調整。"],"optionsEn":["The plastic-hinge length is simply the cracked length at the column base and can be measured on site.","Plastic deformation actually spreads over a zone at the column base.","A few centimetres of extra hoop spacing do not affect safety and can be adjusted for site convenience."],"answer":1,"explanation":"實際塑性變形分布在柱底一段區域內，為了計算方便，以等效塑鉸長度 L_p 把曲率集中成一個轉角：L_p 一部分來自柱高（彎矩梯度），一部分來自主筋在基礎中的應變滲透，因此與主筋直徑及降伏強度有關。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Plastic deformation actually spreads over a zone at the column base; for convenience an equivalent plastic-hinge length L_p concentrates curvature into one rotation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b047-v13-14","title":"塑鉸長度、轉角容量與搭接禁區：定量估算","titleEn":"Hinge length, rotation capacity and no-splice zones: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「塑鉸長度 L_p」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Plastic-hinge length L_p” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：等效塑鉸長度 L_p = 0.08·L + 0.022·f_ye·d_bl = 0.08×10 + 0.022×475×0.036 ≈ 1.18 m（不小於 0.044·f_ye·d_bl ≈ 0.75 m）。中性軸深 c = 0.25·D = 0.5 m，φ_u = 0.0136/0.5 ≈ 0.0272 1/m；θ_p = (0.0272 − 0.0027)×1.18 ≈ 0.029 rad；Δ_p = θ_p·(L − L_p/2) ≈ 0.029×9.41 ≈ 0.27 m。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: L_p = 0.08·L + 0.022·f_ye·d_bl = 0.08×10 + 0.022×475×0.036 ≈ 1.18 m (not less than 0.044·f_ye·d_bl ≈ 0.75 m). With neutral-axis depth c = 0.25·D = 0.5 m, φ_u = 0.0136/0.5 ≈ 0.0272 1/m; θ_p = (0.0272 − 0.0027)×1.18 ≈ 0.029 rad; Δ_p = θ_p·(L − L_p/2) ≈ 0.029×9.41 ≈ 0.27 m. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比對手算與推覆分析的容量位移，並確認圖面上的塑鉸區範圍（通常取 L_p、斷面尺寸與柱高某比例三者中的較大值）內沒有主筋搭接、斷筋或施工縫錯位；續接只能放在塑鉸區外或使用經試驗認可的機械續接器。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare the hand capacity displacement with the pushover result, and confirm that within the hinge-zone extent on the drawings (usually the greatest of L_p, the section dimension and a fraction of column height) there are no lap splices, bar cutoffs or misplaced construction joints; splices go outside the zone or use test-qualified mechanical couplers.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"等效塑鉸長度 L_p = 0.08·L + 0.022·f_ye·d_bl = 0.08×10 + 0.022×475×0.036 ≈ 1.18 m（不小於 0.044·f_ye·d_bl ≈ 0.75 m）。中性軸深 c = 0.25·D = 0.5 m，φ_u = 0.0136/0.5 ≈ 0.0272 1/m；θ_p = (0.0272 − 0.0027)×1.18 ≈ 0.029 rad；Δ_p = θ_p·(L − L_p/2) ≈ 0.029×9.41 ≈ 0.27 m。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"L_p = 0.08·L + 0.022·f_ye·d_bl = 0.08×10 + 0.022×475×0.036 ≈ 1.18 m (not less than 0.044·f_ye·d_bl ≈ 0.75 m). With neutral-axis depth c = 0.25·D = 0.5 m, φ_u = 0.0136/0.5 ≈ 0.0272 1/m; θ_p = (0.0272 − 0.0027)×1.18 ≈ 0.029 rad; Δ_p = θ_p·(L − L_p/2) ≈ 0.029×9.41 ≈ 0.27 m. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「塑鉸長度、轉角容量與搭接禁區」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Hinge length, rotation capacity and no-splice zones\", which statement holds?","options":["單調推到破壞的試驗就足以代表地震下的柱韌性。","耐震與耐久是兩個獨立問題，腐蝕不會影響橋墩的耐震能力。","等效塑鉸長度 L_p = 0.08·L + 0.022·f_ye·d_bl = 0.08×10 + 0.022×475×0.036 ≈ 1.18 m（不小於 0.044·f_ye·d_bl ≈ 0.75 m）。"],"optionsEn":["A monotonic push to failure is enough to represent column ductility under earthquakes.","Seismic and durability performance are separate issues; corrosion does not affect a pier's seismic capacity.","L_p = 0.08·L + 0.022·f_ye·d_bl = 0.08×10 + 0.022×475×0.036 ≈ 1.18 m (not less than 0.044·f_ye·d_bl ≈ 0.75 m)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"等效塑鉸長度 L_p = 0.08·L + 0.022·f_ye·d_bl = 0.08×10 + 0.022×475×0.036 ≈ 1.18 m（不小於 0.044·f_ye·d_bl ≈ 0.75 m）。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"L_p = 0.08·L + 0.022·f_ye·d_bl = 0.08×10 + 0.022×475×0.036 ≈ 1.18 m (not less than 0.044·f_ye·d_bl ≈ 0.75 m). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b047-v13-15","title":"塑鉸長度、轉角容量與搭接禁區：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Hinge length, rotation capacity and no-splice zones: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「塑鉸長度 L_p」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Plastic-hinge length L_p” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比對手算與推覆分析的容量位移，並確認圖面上的塑鉸區範圍（通常取 L_p、斷面尺寸與柱高某比例三者中的較大值）內沒有主筋搭接、斷筋或施工縫錯位；續接只能放在塑鉸區外或使用經試驗認可的機械續接器。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare the hand capacity displacement with the pushover result, and confirm that within the hinge-zone extent on the drawings (usually the greatest of L_p, the section dimension and a fraction of column height) there are no lap splices, bar cutoffs or misplaced construction joints; splices go outside the zone or use test-qualified mechanical couplers. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：柱主筋優先採用通長或塑鉸區外的機械續接，基礎內錨定長度與彎鉤方向依設計圖施作；施工前召開配筋協調會，確認塑鉸區、施工縫與續接位置。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prefer continuous column bars or mechanical couplers outside the hinge zone, and build footing anchorage length and hook direction exactly as drawn; hold a reinforcement coordination meeting before construction to confirm hinge-zone, construction-joint and splice locations.","failure":"注意干擾：舊橋常在柱底以短搭接連接基礎預留筋，地震時搭接段滑脫，柱底彎矩強度驟降並形成搖擺；主筋在柱中段截斷時，塑鉸可能轉移到截斷點而該處缺乏圍束，造成意外的剪力或彎曲破壞。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Older piers often lap column bars onto short footing starter bars at the base; in an earthquake the splice slips, base moment strength collapses and the column rocks; where bars are cut off at mid-height, the hinge can migrate to the cutoff point, which lacks confinement, causing unexpected shear or flexural failure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比對手算與推覆分析的容量位移，並確認圖面上的塑鉸區範圍（通常取 L_p、斷面尺寸與柱高某比例三者中的較大值）內沒有主筋搭接、斷筋或施工縫錯位；續接只能放在塑鉸區外或使用經試驗認可的機械續接器。","textEn":"Compare the hand capacity displacement with the pushover result, and confirm that within the hinge-zone extent on the drawings (usually the greatest of L_p, the section dimension and a fraction of column height) there are no lap splices, bar cutoffs or misplaced construction joints; splices go outside the zone or use test-qualified mechanical couplers.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"柱主筋優先採用通長或塑鉸區外的機械續接，基礎內錨定長度與彎鉤方向依設計圖施作；施工前召開配筋協調會，確認塑鉸區、施工縫與續接位置。","textEn":"Prefer continuous column bars or mechanical couplers outside the hinge zone, and build footing anchorage length and hook direction exactly as drawn; hold a reinforcement coordination meeting before construction to confirm hinge-zone, construction-joint and splice locations.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「塑鉸長度、轉角容量與搭接禁區」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Hinge length, rotation capacity and no-splice zones\"?","options":["比對手算與推覆分析的容量位移，並確認圖面上的塑鉸區範圍（通常取 L_p、斷面尺寸與柱高某比例三者中的較大值）內沒有主筋搭接、斷筋或施工縫錯位。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","橋墩越強越好，所有構件都加強就能確保耐震安全。"],"optionsEn":["Compare the hand capacity displacement with the pushover result, and confirm that within the hinge-zone extent on the drawings (usually the greatest of L_p, the section dimension and a fraction of column height) there are no lap splices, bar cutoffs or misplaced construction joints.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The stronger the pier the better; strengthening every member guarantees seismic safety."],"answer":0,"explanation":"比對手算與推覆分析的容量位移，並確認圖面上的塑鉸區範圍（通常取 L_p、斷面尺寸與柱高某比例三者中的較大值）內沒有主筋搭接、斷筋或施工縫錯位；續接只能放在塑鉸區外或使用經試驗認可的機械續接器。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare the hand capacity displacement with the pushover result, and confirm that within the hinge-zone extent on the drawings (usually the greatest of L_p, the section dimension and a fraction of column height) there are no lap splices, bar cutoffs or misplaced construction joints; splices go outside the zone or use test-qualified mechanical couplers. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b047-v13-16","title":"塑鉸長度、轉角容量與搭接禁區：失效診斷","titleEn":"Hinge length, rotation capacity and no-splice zones: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「塑鉸長度 L_p」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Plastic-hinge length L_p” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"舊橋常在柱底以短搭接連接基礎預留筋，地震時搭接段滑脫，柱底彎矩強度驟降並形成搖擺；主筋在柱中段截斷時，塑鉸可能轉移到截斷點而該處缺乏圍束，造成意外的剪力或彎曲破壞。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Older piers often lap column bars onto short footing starter bars at the base; in an earthquake the splice slips, base moment strength collapses and the column rocks; where bars are cut off at mid-height, the hinge can migrate to the cutoff point, which lacks confinement, causing unexpected shear or flexural failure. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：塑鉸區內不允許主筋搭接，因為搭接在反覆大應變下會滑脫，這正是許多早期橋墩在柱底搭接處破壞的原因。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Lap splices are not allowed in the hinge zone because they slip under reversed large strains, which is why many older piers failed at base lap splices.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「塑鉸長度就是柱底出現裂縫的長度，可以在現場直接量到。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The plastic-hinge length is simply the cracked length at the column base and can be measured on site.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"舊橋常在柱底以短搭接連接基礎預留筋，地震時搭接段滑脫，柱底彎矩強度驟降並形成搖擺；主筋在柱中段截斷時，塑鉸可能轉移到截斷點而該處缺乏圍束，造成意外的剪力或彎曲破壞。","textEn":"Older piers often lap column bars onto short footing starter bars at the base; in an earthquake the splice slips, base moment strength collapses and the column rocks; where bars are cut off at mid-height, the hinge can migrate to the cutoff point, which lacks confinement, causing unexpected shear or flexural failure.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「塑鉸長度、轉角容量與搭接禁區」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Hinge length, rotation capacity and no-splice zones\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","舊橋常在柱底以短搭接連接基礎預留筋，地震時搭接段滑脫，柱底彎矩強度驟降並形成搖擺。","箍筋間距差幾公分不影響結構安全，可以依現場方便調整。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Older piers often lap column bars onto short footing starter bars at the base.","A few centimetres of extra hoop spacing do not affect safety and can be adjusted for site convenience."],"answer":1,"explanation":"舊橋常在柱底以短搭接連接基礎預留筋，地震時搭接段滑脫，柱底彎矩強度驟降並形成搖擺；主筋在柱中段截斷時，塑鉸可能轉移到截斷點而該處缺乏圍束，造成意外的剪力或彎曲破壞。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Older piers often lap column bars onto short footing starter bars at the base; in an earthquake the splice slips, base moment strength collapses and the column rocks; where bars are cut off at mid-height, the hinge can migrate to the cutoff point, which lacks confinement, causing unexpected shear or flexural failure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b047-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「塑鉸區鋼筋施工與查驗」與「續接器、錨定與接頭施工」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Hinge-zone reinforcement construction and inspection\" and \"Couplers, anchorage and joint construction\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b047-v13-17","title":"塑鉸區鋼筋施工與查驗：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Hinge-zone reinforcement construction and inspection: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「箍筋間距查驗」如何影響橋墩塑鉸韌性設計的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Hoop spacing inspection” governs force, deformation or durability in “Ductile plastic-hinge design for bridge piers”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"塑鉸區配筋最密：大直徑主筋、密集螺旋筋、繫筋與基礎頂層筋交錯，模板內空間有限，施工者常為了方便澆置而放寬箍筋間距、縮短彎鉤或省略繫筋，這些小變更都直接降低圍束效果。混凝土方面，粒料粒徑與坍度必須讓混凝土流過密集鋼筋並充分搗實，否則柱底出現蜂窩，保護層與核心之間的握裹不良。施工縫若設在塑鉸區內，界面也會成為弱面。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「箍筋間距查驗」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The hinge zone has the densest reinforcement: large longitudinal bars, closely spaced spirals, cross-ties and the footing's top mat all intersect in limited form space, and contractors are tempted to widen hoop spacing, shorten hooks or omit cross-ties for easier placing, each of which directly reduces confinement. For concrete, aggregate size and slump must let it flow through congested steel and be fully compacted, or honeycombing appears at the column base with poor bond between cover and core. A construction joint placed within the hinge zone also becomes a plane of weakness. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Hoop spacing inspection” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：螺旋筋體積比與間距成反比，ρ_s ∝ 1/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: ρ_s ∝ 1/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「箍筋間距差幾公分不影響結構安全，可以依現場方便調整。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A few centimetres of extra hoop spacing do not affect safety and can be adjusted for site convenience.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「箍筋間距查驗」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Hoop spacing inspection”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-17-k1","title":"塑鉸區鋼筋施工與查驗","titleEn":"Hinge-zone reinforcement construction and inspection","text":"塑鉸區配筋最密：大直徑主筋、密集螺旋筋、繫筋與基礎頂層筋交錯，模板內空間有限，施工者常為了方便澆置而放寬箍筋間距、縮短彎鉤或省略繫筋，這些小變更都直接降低圍束效果。混凝土方面，粒料粒徑與坍度必須讓混凝土流過密集鋼筋並充分搗實，否則柱底出現蜂窩，保護層與核心之間的握裹不良。","textEn":"The hinge zone has the densest reinforcement: large longitudinal bars, closely spaced spirals, cross-ties and the footing's top mat all intersect in limited form space, and contractors are tempted to widen hoop spacing, shorten hooks or omit cross-ties for easier placing, each of which directly reduces confinement. For concrete, aggregate size and slump must let it flow through congested steel and be fully compacted, or honeycombing appears at the column base with poor bond between cover and core.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：箍筋間距差幾公分不影響結構安全，可以依現場方便調整。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A few centimetres of extra hoop spacing do not affect safety and can be adjusted for site convenience. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「塑鉸區鋼筋施工與查驗」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Hinge-zone reinforcement construction and inspection\" is correct?","options":["箍筋間距差幾公分不影響結構安全，可以依現場方便調整。","只要續接器能承受鋼筋的降伏強度，就可以用在塑鉸區。","塑鉸區配筋最密：大直徑主筋、密集螺旋筋、繫筋與基礎頂層筋交錯，模板內空間有限，施工者常為了方便澆置而放寬箍筋間距、縮短彎鉤或省略繫筋，這些小變更都直接降低圍束效果。"],"optionsEn":["A few centimetres of extra hoop spacing do not affect safety and can be adjusted for site convenience.","Any coupler that develops the bar's yield strength can be used in a plastic hinge zone.","The hinge zone has the densest reinforcement: large longitudinal bars, closely spaced spirals, cross-ties and the footing's top mat all intersect in limited form space, and contractors are tempted to widen hoop spacing, shorten hooks or omit cross-ties for easier placing, each of which directly reduces confinement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"塑鉸區配筋最密：大直徑主筋、密集螺旋筋、繫筋與基礎頂層筋交錯，模板內空間有限，施工者常為了方便澆置而放寬箍筋間距、縮短彎鉤或省略繫筋，這些小變更都直接降低圍束效果。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The hinge zone has the densest reinforcement: large longitudinal bars, closely spaced spirals, cross-ties and the footing's top mat all intersect in limited form space, and contractors are tempted to widen hoop spacing, shorten hooks or omit cross-ties for easier placing, each of which directly reduces confinement. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b047-v13-18","title":"塑鉸區鋼筋施工與查驗：定量估算","titleEn":"Hinge-zone reinforcement construction and inspection: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「箍筋間距查驗」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Hoop spacing inspection” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：螺旋筋體積比與間距成反比，ρ_s ∝ 1/s。設計間距 s = 100 mm、ρ_s = 0.0080；若現場放寬為 130 mm，ρ_s = 1,520/(1,900×130) ≈ 0.0062，下降約 23%；ε_cu 由 0.0136 降為 0.004 + 1.4×0.0062×475×0.09/50 ≈ 0.0114，約下降 16%，轉角容量隨之降低。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: ρ_s ∝ 1/s. With s = 100 mm, ρ_s = 0.0080; if widened on site to 130 mm, ρ_s = 1,520/(1,900×130) ≈ 0.0062, about 23% lower; ε_cu falls from 0.0136 to 0.004 + 1.4×0.0062×475×0.09/50 ≈ 0.0114, about 16% lower, and rotation capacity drops accordingly. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：澆置前由監造逐支柱量測塑鉸區箍筋間距、彎鉤角度與延伸長度、繫筋數量與保護層，以照片與量尺記錄；混凝土採用可通過鋼筋淨距的粒料尺寸，並在試拌時確認流動性；拆模後檢查柱底是否有蜂窩。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before casting, the inspector measures each column's hinge-zone hoop spacing, hook angle and extension, cross-tie count and cover, recording with photos and a tape; the concrete uses an aggregate size that passes the bar clear spacing with flowability confirmed in trial mixes; after stripping inspect the column base for honeycombing.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"螺旋筋體積比與間距成反比，ρ_s ∝ 1/s。設計間距 s = 100 mm、ρ_s = 0.0080；若現場放寬為 130 mm，ρ_s = 1,520/(1,900×130) ≈ 0.0062，下降約 23%；ε_cu 由 0.0136 降為 0.004 + 1.4×0.0062×475×0.09/50 ≈ 0.0114，約下降 16%，轉角容量隨之降低。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"ρ_s ∝ 1/s. With s = 100 mm, ρ_s = 0.0080; if widened on site to 130 mm, ρ_s = 1,520/(1,900×130) ≈ 0.0062, about 23% lower; ε_cu falls from 0.0136 to 0.004 + 1.4×0.0062×475×0.09/50 ≈ 0.0114, about 16% lower, and rotation capacity drops accordingly. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「塑鉸區鋼筋施工與查驗」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Hinge-zone reinforcement construction and inspection\", which statement holds?","options":["螺旋筋體積比與間距成反比，ρ_s ∝ 1/s。","震後柱子沒有倒，就表示可以直接恢復通行。","混凝土剪力強度是固定值，不會因柱子的彎曲變形而改變。"],"optionsEn":["ρ_s ∝ 1/s.","If a column did not collapse in the earthquake, the bridge can reopen immediately.","The concrete shear strength is a fixed value that does not change with column flexural deformation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"螺旋筋體積比與間距成反比，ρ_s ∝ 1/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"ρ_s ∝ 1/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b047-v13-19","title":"塑鉸區鋼筋施工與查驗：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Hinge-zone reinforcement construction and inspection: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「箍筋間距查驗」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Hoop spacing inspection” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"澆置前由監造逐支柱量測塑鉸區箍筋間距、彎鉤角度與延伸長度、繫筋數量與保護層，以照片與量尺記錄；混凝土採用可通過鋼筋淨距的粒料尺寸，並在試拌時確認流動性；拆模後檢查柱底是否有蜂窩。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before casting, the inspector measures each column's hinge-zone hoop spacing, hook angle and extension, cross-tie count and cover, recording with photos and a tape; the concrete uses an aggregate size that passes the bar clear spacing with flowability confirmed in trial mixes; after stripping inspect the column base for honeycombing. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把塑鉸區配筋查驗列為澆置前的停留點，未經監造簽認不得澆置；任何配筋變更（間距、彎鉤、續接）須經設計者書面同意，並記入竣工圖。","observationEn":"Site practice: Make hinge-zone reinforcement inspection a hold point before casting that cannot be passed without the inspector's signature; any change to spacing, hooks or splices needs the designer's written approval and goes into the as-built drawings.","failure":"注意干擾：箍筋間距在施工中被放寬、彎鉤只做 90 度或繫筋遺漏，地震時保護層剝落後箍筋彎鉤張開，核心混凝土失去圍束，主筋挫屈；這種缺陷在完工後完全被混凝土覆蓋，只有大地震才會暴露。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Hoop spacing widened during construction, 90-degree hooks or missing cross-ties let hooks open once the cover spalls in an earthquake, so the core loses confinement and bars buckle; such defects are completely hidden by concrete after completion and are exposed only by a major earthquake. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"澆置前由監造逐支柱量測塑鉸區箍筋間距、彎鉤角度與延伸長度、繫筋數量與保護層，以照片與量尺記錄；混凝土採用可通過鋼筋淨距的粒料尺寸，並在試拌時確認流動性；拆模後檢查柱底是否有蜂窩。","textEn":"Before casting, the inspector measures each column's hinge-zone hoop spacing, hook angle and extension, cross-tie count and cover, recording with photos and a tape; the concrete uses an aggregate size that passes the bar clear spacing with flowability confirmed in trial mixes; after stripping inspect the column base for honeycombing.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把塑鉸區配筋查驗列為澆置前的停留點，未經監造簽認不得澆置；任何配筋變更（間距、彎鉤、續接）須經設計者書面同意，並記入竣工圖。","textEn":"Make hinge-zone reinforcement inspection a hold point before casting that cannot be passed without the inspector's signature; any change to spacing, hooks or splices needs the designer's written approval and goes into the as-built drawings.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「塑鉸區鋼筋施工與查驗」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Hinge-zone reinforcement construction and inspection\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","澆置前由監造逐支柱量測塑鉸區箍筋間距、彎鉤角度與延伸長度、繫筋數量與保護層，以照片與量尺記錄。","只要強度需求以韌性折減後滿足，就不必檢查位移。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Before casting, the inspector measures each column's hinge-zone hoop spacing, hook angle and extension, cross-tie count and cover, recording with photos and a tape.","If strength demand reduced by ductility is satisfied, displacement need not be checked."],"answer":1,"explanation":"澆置前由監造逐支柱量測塑鉸區箍筋間距、彎鉤角度與延伸長度、繫筋數量與保護層，以照片與量尺記錄；混凝土採用可通過鋼筋淨距的粒料尺寸，並在試拌時確認流動性；拆模後檢查柱底是否有蜂窩。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before casting, the inspector measures each column's hinge-zone hoop spacing, hook angle and extension, cross-tie count and cover, recording with photos and a tape; the concrete uses an aggregate size that passes the bar clear spacing with flowability confirmed in trial mixes; after stripping inspect the column base for honeycombing. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b047-v13-20","title":"塑鉸區鋼筋施工與查驗：失效診斷","titleEn":"Hinge-zone reinforcement construction and inspection: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「箍筋間距查驗」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Hoop spacing inspection” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"箍筋間距在施工中被放寬、彎鉤只做 90 度或繫筋遺漏，地震時保護層剝落後箍筋彎鉤張開，核心混凝土失去圍束，主筋挫屈；這種缺陷在完工後完全被混凝土覆蓋，只有大地震才會暴露。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Hoop spacing widened during construction, 90-degree hooks or missing cross-ties let hooks open once the cover spalls in an earthquake, so the core loses confinement and bars buckle; such defects are completely hidden by concrete after completion and are exposed only by a major earthquake. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：施工縫若設在塑鉸區內，界面也會成為弱面。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A construction joint placed within the hinge zone also becomes a plane of weakness.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「箍筋間距差幾公分不影響結構安全，可以依現場方便調整。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A few centimetres of extra hoop spacing do not affect safety and can be adjusted for site convenience.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"箍筋間距在施工中被放寬、彎鉤只做 90 度或繫筋遺漏，地震時保護層剝落後箍筋彎鉤張開，核心混凝土失去圍束，主筋挫屈；這種缺陷在完工後完全被混凝土覆蓋，只有大地震才會暴露。","textEn":"Hoop spacing widened during construction, 90-degree hooks or missing cross-ties let hooks open once the cover spalls in an earthquake, so the core loses confinement and bars buckle; such defects are completely hidden by concrete after completion and are exposed only by a major earthquake.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「塑鉸區鋼筋施工與查驗」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Hinge-zone reinforcement construction and inspection\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","只要續接器能承受鋼筋的降伏強度，就可以用在塑鉸區。","箍筋間距在施工中被放寬、彎鉤只做 90 度或繫筋遺漏，地震時保護層剝落後箍筋彎鉤張開，核心混凝土失去圍束，主筋挫屈。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Any coupler that develops the bar's yield strength can be used in a plastic hinge zone.","Hoop spacing widened during construction, 90-degree hooks or missing cross-ties let hooks open once the cover spalls in an earthquake, so the core loses confinement and bars buckle."],"answer":2,"explanation":"箍筋間距在施工中被放寬、彎鉤只做 90 度或繫筋遺漏，地震時保護層剝落後箍筋彎鉤張開，核心混凝土失去圍束，主筋挫屈；這種缺陷在完工後完全被混凝土覆蓋，只有大地震才會暴露。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Hoop spacing widened during construction, 90-degree hooks or missing cross-ties let hooks open once the cover spalls in an earthquake, so the core loses confinement and bars buckle; such defects are completely hidden by concrete after completion and are exposed only by a major earthquake. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b047-v13-21","title":"續接器、錨定與接頭施工：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Couplers, anchorage and joint construction: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「機械續接器與基礎錨定」如何影響橋墩塑鉸韌性設計的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Mechanical couplers and footing anchorage” governs force, deformation or durability in “Ductile plastic-hinge design for bridge piers”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"柱主筋要在塑鉸區發展到超過降伏的大應變，因此續接與錨定必須比鋼筋本身更強：機械續接器要能讓鋼筋在續接器外降伏並硬化，而不是在續接器內拉脫；主筋伸入基礎或帽梁的長度與彎鉤方向，要確保塑鉸應變滲透段不會拔出。梁柱接頭內鋼筋交錯最密，接頭剪力需要專門的箍筋與垂直筋，施工順序也要讓接頭混凝土能一次澆置密實。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「機械續接器與基礎錨定」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Column bars must develop strains well beyond yield in the hinge zone, so splices and anchorages must be stronger than the bars: a mechanical coupler must let the bar yield and strain-harden outside the coupler rather than pull out inside it, and the length and hook direction of bars extending into the footing or cap beam must ensure the strain-penetration zone does not pull out. Beam–column joints have the most congested steel; joint shear needs dedicated hoops and vertical bars, and the construction sequence must let joint concrete be placed densely in one pour. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Mechanical couplers and footing anchorage” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：36 mm 主筋面積 A_b = π×18² ≈ 1,018 mm²；若要求續接器在鋼筋拉力達 620 MPa（教學取期望抗拉強度）前不破壞，所需能力 F = 1,018×620 ≈ 631 kN；試驗若在 590 kN 時於續接器內滑脫，只達需求的 94%，判定不合格。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A 36 mm bar has A_b = π×18² ≈ 1,018 mm²; if a coupler must not fail before the bar reaches 620 MPa (taken here as expected tensile strength), the required capacity is F = 1,018×620 ≈ 631 kN; a test that slips inside the coupler at 590 kN reaches only 94% of demand and fails acceptance.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要續接器能承受鋼筋的降伏強度，就可以用在塑鉸區。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Any coupler that develops the bar's yield strength can be used in a plastic hinge zone.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「機械續接器與基礎錨定」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Mechanical couplers and footing anchorage”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-21-k1","title":"續接器、錨定與接頭施工","titleEn":"Couplers, anchorage and joint construction","text":"柱主筋要在塑鉸區發展到超過降伏的大應變，因此續接與錨定必須比鋼筋本身更強：機械續接器要能讓鋼筋在續接器外降伏並硬化，而不是在續接器內拉脫；主筋伸入基礎或帽梁的長度與彎鉤方向，要確保塑鉸應變滲透段不會拔出。梁柱接頭內鋼筋交錯最密，接頭剪力需要專門的箍筋與垂直筋，施工順序也要讓接頭混凝土能一次澆置密實。","textEn":"Column bars must develop strains well beyond yield in the hinge zone, so splices and anchorages must be stronger than the bars: a mechanical coupler must let the bar yield and strain-harden outside the coupler rather than pull out inside it, and the length and hook direction of bars extending into the footing or cap beam must ensure the strain-penetration zone does not pull out. Beam–column joints have the most congested steel; joint shear needs dedicated hoops and vertical bars, and the construction sequence must let joint concrete be placed densely in one pour.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要續接器能承受鋼筋的降伏強度，就可以用在塑鉸區。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Any coupler that develops the bar's yield strength can be used in a plastic hinge zone. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「續接器、錨定與接頭施工」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Couplers, anchorage and joint construction\" is correct?","options":["柱主筋要在塑鉸區發展到超過降伏的大應變，因此續接與錨定必須比鋼筋本身更強：機械續接器要能讓鋼筋在續接器外降伏並硬化，而不是在續接器內拉脫。","只要續接器能承受鋼筋的降伏強度，就可以用在塑鉸區。","單調推到破壞的試驗就足以代表地震下的柱韌性。"],"optionsEn":["Column bars must develop strains well beyond yield in the hinge zone, so splices and anchorages must be stronger than the bars: a mechanical coupler must let the bar yield and strain-harden outside the coupler rather than pull out inside it, and the length and hook direction of bars extending into the footing or cap beam must ensure the strain-penetration zone does not pull out.","Any coupler that develops the bar's yield strength can be used in a plastic hinge zone.","A monotonic push to failure is enough to represent column ductility under earthquakes."],"answer":0,"explanation":"柱主筋要在塑鉸區發展到超過降伏的大應變，因此續接與錨定必須比鋼筋本身更強：機械續接器要能讓鋼筋在續接器外降伏並硬化，而不是在續接器內拉脫；主筋伸入基礎或帽梁的長度與彎鉤方向，要確保塑鉸應變滲透段不會拔出。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Column bars must develop strains well beyond yield in the hinge zone, so splices and anchorages must be stronger than the bars: a mechanical coupler must let the bar yield and strain-harden outside the coupler rather than pull out inside it, and the length and hook direction of bars extending into the footing or cap beam must ensure the strain-penetration zone does not pull out. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b047-v13-22","title":"續接器、錨定與接頭施工：定量估算","titleEn":"Couplers, anchorage and joint construction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「機械續接器與基礎錨定」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Mechanical couplers and footing anchorage” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：36 mm 主筋面積 A_b = π×18² ≈ 1,018 mm²；若要求續接器在鋼筋拉力達 620 MPa（教學取期望抗拉強度）前不破壞，所需能力 F = 1,018×620 ≈ 631 kN；試驗若在 590 kN 時於續接器內滑脫，只達需求的 94%，判定不合格。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A 36 mm bar has A_b = π×18² ≈ 1,018 mm²; if a coupler must not fail before the bar reaches 620 MPa (taken here as expected tensile strength), the required capacity is F = 1,018×620 ≈ 631 kN; a test that slips inside the coupler at 590 kN reaches only 94% of demand and fails acceptance. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：續接器須有型式試驗證明可發展鋼筋的期望抗拉強度與足夠延性，並在現場抽樣做拉力試驗；安裝時檢查鋼筋插入深度標記與鎖緊扭力，梁柱接頭澆置前檢查接頭箍筋與錨定長度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Couplers need type-test evidence that they develop the bar's expected tensile strength with adequate ductility, plus site sample tension tests; during installation check bar insertion marks and tightening torque, and before casting the joint check joint hoops and anchorage lengths.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"36 mm 主筋面積 A_b = π×18² ≈ 1,018 mm²；若要求續接器在鋼筋拉力達 620 MPa（教學取期望抗拉強度）前不破壞，所需能力 F = 1,018×620 ≈ 631 kN；試驗若在 590 kN 時於續接器內滑脫，只達需求的 94%，判定不合格。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"A 36 mm bar has A_b = π×18² ≈ 1,018 mm²; if a coupler must not fail before the bar reaches 620 MPa (taken here as expected tensile strength), the required capacity is F = 1,018×620 ≈ 631 kN; a test that slips inside the coupler at 590 kN reaches only 94% of demand and fails acceptance. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「續接器、錨定與接頭施工」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Couplers, anchorage and joint construction\", which statement holds?","options":["耐震與耐久是兩個獨立問題，腐蝕不會影響橋墩的耐震能力。","36 mm 主筋面積 A_b = π×18² ≈ 1,018 mm²。","橋墩越強越好，所有構件都加強就能確保耐震安全。"],"optionsEn":["Seismic and durability performance are separate issues; corrosion does not affect a pier's seismic capacity.","A 36 mm bar has A_b = π×18² ≈ 1,018 mm².","The stronger the pier the better; strengthening every member guarantees seismic safety."],"answer":1,"explanation":"36 mm 主筋面積 A_b = π×18² ≈ 1,018 mm²；若要求續接器在鋼筋拉力達 620 MPa（教學取期望抗拉強度）前不破壞，所需能力 F = 1,018×620 ≈ 631 kN；試驗若在 590 kN 時於續接器內滑脫，只達需求的 94%，判定不合格。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A 36 mm bar has A_b = π×18² ≈ 1,018 mm²; if a coupler must not fail before the bar reaches 620 MPa (taken here as expected tensile strength), the required capacity is F = 1,018×620 ≈ 631 kN; a test that slips inside the coupler at 590 kN reaches only 94% of demand and fails acceptance. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b047-v13-23","title":"續接器、錨定與接頭施工：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Couplers, anchorage and joint construction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「機械續接器與基礎錨定」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Mechanical couplers and footing anchorage” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"續接器須有型式試驗證明可發展鋼筋的期望抗拉強度與足夠延性，並在現場抽樣做拉力試驗；安裝時檢查鋼筋插入深度標記與鎖緊扭力，梁柱接頭澆置前檢查接頭箍筋與錨定長度。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Couplers need type-test evidence that they develop the bar's expected tensile strength with adequate ductility, plus site sample tension tests; during installation check bar insertion marks and tightening torque, and before casting the joint check joint hoops and anchorage lengths. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：規格書區分「一般續接」與「可用於塑鉸區的高等級續接」，後者須附型式試驗、批次證明與現場抽樣拉力報告；梁柱接頭配筋以三維圖或實體模型預先檢查可施工性。","observationEn":"Site practice: The specification distinguishes ordinary splices from high-grade splices allowed in hinge zones, the latter requiring type tests, batch certificates and site sample tension reports; check beam–column joint reinforcement for buildability in advance with 3D drawings or a physical mock-up.","failure":"注意干擾：使用只能達到鋼筋降伏強度的一般續接器，大地震時鋼筋硬化後拉力超過續接器能力，在續接器處拉斷或拔出，塑鉸無法發展完整轉角；梁柱接頭剪力不足時，接頭先開裂破壞，與賽普勒斯高架橋接頭區的教訓一致。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ordinary couplers that only develop the bar's yield strength fail by fracture or pull-out once the bars strain-harden in a major earthquake, so the hinge cannot develop full rotation; inadequate joint shear capacity lets the joint crack and fail first, consistent with the joint-region lessons of the Cypress Viaduct. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"續接器須有型式試驗證明可發展鋼筋的期望抗拉強度與足夠延性，並在現場抽樣做拉力試驗；安裝時檢查鋼筋插入深度標記與鎖緊扭力，梁柱接頭澆置前檢查接頭箍筋與錨定長度。","textEn":"Couplers need type-test evidence that they develop the bar's expected tensile strength with adequate ductility, plus site sample tension tests; during installation check bar insertion marks and tightening torque, and before casting the joint check joint hoops and anchorage lengths.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"規格書區分「一般續接」與「可用於塑鉸區的高等級續接」，後者須附型式試驗、批次證明與現場抽樣拉力報告；梁柱接頭配筋以三維圖或實體模型預先檢查可施工性。","textEn":"The specification distinguishes ordinary splices from high-grade splices allowed in hinge zones, the latter requiring type tests, batch certificates and site sample tension reports; check beam–column joint reinforcement for buildability in advance with 3D drawings or a physical mock-up.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「續接器、錨定與接頭施工」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Couplers, anchorage and joint construction\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","箍筋主要是用來固定主筋位置，對耐震性能影響不大。","續接器須有型式試驗證明可發展鋼筋的期望抗拉強度與足夠延性，並在現場抽樣做拉力試驗；安裝時檢查鋼筋插入深度標記與鎖緊扭力，梁柱接頭澆置前檢查接頭箍筋與錨定長度。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Hoops mainly hold the longitudinal bars in place and matter little for seismic performance.","Couplers need type-test evidence that they develop the bar's expected tensile strength with adequate ductility, plus site sample tension tests."],"answer":2,"explanation":"續接器須有型式試驗證明可發展鋼筋的期望抗拉強度與足夠延性，並在現場抽樣做拉力試驗；安裝時檢查鋼筋插入深度標記與鎖緊扭力，梁柱接頭澆置前檢查接頭箍筋與錨定長度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Couplers need type-test evidence that they develop the bar's expected tensile strength with adequate ductility, plus site sample tension tests; during installation check bar insertion marks and tightening torque, and before casting the joint check joint hoops and anchorage lengths. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b047-v13-24","title":"續接器、錨定與接頭施工：失效診斷","titleEn":"Couplers, anchorage and joint construction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「機械續接器與基礎錨定」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Mechanical couplers and footing anchorage” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"使用只能達到鋼筋降伏強度的一般續接器，大地震時鋼筋硬化後拉力超過續接器能力，在續接器處拉斷或拔出，塑鉸無法發展完整轉角；梁柱接頭剪力不足時，接頭先開裂破壞，與賽普勒斯高架橋接頭區的教訓一致。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ordinary couplers that only develop the bar's yield strength fail by fracture or pull-out once the bars strain-harden in a major earthquake, so the hinge cannot develop full rotation; inadequate joint shear capacity lets the joint crack and fail first, consistent with the joint-region lessons of the Cypress Viaduct. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：梁柱接頭內鋼筋交錯最密，接頭剪力需要專門的箍筋與垂直筋，施工順序也要讓接頭混凝土能一次澆置密實。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Beam–column joints have the most congested steel; joint shear needs dedicated hoops and vertical bars, and the construction sequence must let joint concrete be placed densely in one pour.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要續接器能承受鋼筋的降伏強度，就可以用在塑鉸區。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Any coupler that develops the bar's yield strength can be used in a plastic hinge zone.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"使用只能達到鋼筋降伏強度的一般續接器，大地震時鋼筋硬化後拉力超過續接器能力，在續接器處拉斷或拔出，塑鉸無法發展完整轉角；梁柱接頭剪力不足時，接頭先開裂破壞，與賽普勒斯高架橋接頭區的教訓一致。","textEn":"Ordinary couplers that only develop the bar's yield strength fail by fracture or pull-out once the bars strain-harden in a major earthquake, so the hinge cannot develop full rotation; inadequate joint shear capacity lets the joint crack and fail first, consistent with the joint-region lessons of the Cypress Viaduct.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「續接器、錨定與接頭施工」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Couplers, anchorage and joint construction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["使用只能達到鋼筋降伏強度的一般續接器，大地震時鋼筋硬化後拉力超過續接器能力，在續接器處拉斷或拔出，塑鉸無法發展完整轉角。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","單調推到破壞的試驗就足以代表地震下的柱韌性。"],"optionsEn":["Ordinary couplers that only develop the bar's yield strength fail by fracture or pull-out once the bars strain-harden in a major earthquake, so the hinge cannot develop full rotation.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","A monotonic push to failure is enough to represent column ductility under earthquakes."],"answer":0,"explanation":"使用只能達到鋼筋降伏強度的一般續接器，大地震時鋼筋硬化後拉力超過續接器能力，在續接器處拉斷或拔出，塑鉸無法發展完整轉角；梁柱接頭剪力不足時，接頭先開裂破壞，與賽普勒斯高架橋接頭區的教訓一致。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ordinary couplers that only develop the bar's yield strength fail by fracture or pull-out once the bars strain-harden in a major earthquake, so the hinge cannot develop full rotation; inadequate joint shear capacity lets the joint crack and fail first, consistent with the joint-region lessons of the Cypress Viaduct. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b047-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「擬靜態反覆載重試驗」與「震後損傷量測與殘留變形」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Quasi-static cyclic column testing\" and \"Post-earthquake damage measurement and residual deformation\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b047-v13-25","title":"擬靜態反覆載重試驗：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Quasi-static cyclic column testing: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「反覆載重遲滯迴圈」如何影響橋墩塑鉸韌性設計的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cyclic hysteresis loops” governs force, deformation or durability in “Ductile plastic-hinge design for bridge piers”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"塑鉸設計公式來自大量柱試體的反覆載重試驗：在固定軸力下，以逐級增加的層間位移角（漂移比）反覆推拉柱頂，每級重複數圈，記錄力—位移遲滯迴圈、裂縫、保護層剝落、主筋挫屈與斷裂的順序。太平洋地震工程研究中心（PEER）的結構性能資料庫收錄了 400 多組反覆載重柱試驗，台灣的國家地震工程研究中心也以反力牆設施進行實尺寸或大比例橋柱試驗。試驗的用途是校驗分析模型與破壞準則，而不是證明單一設計。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「反覆載重遲滯迴圈」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Plastic-hinge design formulas come from many cyclic column tests: under constant axial load the column top is pushed and pulled through increasing drift ratios, several cycles per step, recording hysteresis loops and the sequence of cracking, cover spalling, bar buckling and fracture. The Pacific Earthquake Engineering Research Center's Structural Performance Database holds over 400 cyclic column tests, and Taiwan's NCREE tests full-size or large-scale bridge columns against its reaction wall. Tests calibrate analysis models and failure criteria rather than proving a single design. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Cyclic hysteresis loops” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：1/2.5 縮尺試體柱高 4 m，最大水平力出現在漂移比 1.5%，強度下降到最大值 80% 時漂移比 5.0%，即極限位移 Δ_u = 0.05×4 = 0.20 m；降伏漂移比 0.9%（Δ_y = 0.036 m），位移韌性 μ = 0.20/0.036 ≈ 5.6。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A 1/2.5-scale specimen 4 m tall reaches peak lateral force at 1.5% drift and falls to 80% of peak at 5.0% drift, so ultimate displacement Δ_u = 0.05×4 = 0.20 m; with 0.9% yield drift (Δ_y = 0.036 m), displacement ductility μ = 0.20/0.036 ≈ 5.6.","failure":"常見誤解：「單調推到破壞的試驗就足以代表地震下的柱韌性。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A monotonic push to failure is enough to represent column ductility under earthquakes.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「反覆載重遲滯迴圈」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Cyclic hysteresis loops”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-25-k1","title":"擬靜態反覆載重試驗","titleEn":"Quasi-static cyclic column testing","text":"塑鉸設計公式來自大量柱試體的反覆載重試驗：在固定軸力下，以逐級增加的層間位移角（漂移比）反覆推拉柱頂，每級重複數圈，記錄力—位移遲滯迴圈、裂縫、保護層剝落、主筋挫屈與斷裂的順序。太平洋地震工程研究中心（PEER）的結構性能資料庫收錄了 400 多組反覆載重柱試驗，台灣的國家地震工程研究中心也以反力牆設施進行實尺寸或大比例橋柱試驗。","textEn":"Plastic-hinge design formulas come from many cyclic column tests: under constant axial load the column top is pushed and pulled through increasing drift ratios, several cycles per step, recording hysteresis loops and the sequence of cracking, cover spalling, bar buckling and fracture. The Pacific Earthquake Engineering Research Center's Structural Performance Database holds over 400 cyclic column tests, and Taiwan's NCREE tests full-size or large-scale bridge columns against its reaction wall.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：單調推到破壞的試驗就足以代表地震下的柱韌性。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A monotonic push to failure is enough to represent column ductility under earthquakes. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「擬靜態反覆載重試驗」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Quasi-static cyclic column testing\" is correct?","options":["單調推到破壞的試驗就足以代表地震下的柱韌性。","塑鉸設計公式來自大量柱試體的反覆載重試驗：在固定軸力下，以逐級增加的層間位移角（漂移比）反覆推拉柱頂，每級重複數圈，記錄力—位移遲滯迴圈、裂縫、保護層剝落、主筋挫屈與斷裂的順序。","震後柱子沒有倒，就表示可以直接恢復通行。"],"optionsEn":["A monotonic push to failure is enough to represent column ductility under earthquakes.","Plastic-hinge design formulas come from many cyclic column tests: under constant axial load the column top is pushed and pulled through increasing drift ratios, several cycles per step, recording hysteresis loops and the sequence of cracking, cover spalling, bar buckling and fracture.","If a column did not collapse in the earthquake, the bridge can reopen immediately."],"answer":1,"explanation":"塑鉸設計公式來自大量柱試體的反覆載重試驗：在固定軸力下，以逐級增加的層間位移角（漂移比）反覆推拉柱頂，每級重複數圈，記錄力—位移遲滯迴圈、裂縫、保護層剝落、主筋挫屈與斷裂的順序。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Plastic-hinge design formulas come from many cyclic column tests: under constant axial load the column top is pushed and pulled through increasing drift ratios, several cycles per step, recording hysteresis loops and the sequence of cracking, cover spalling, bar buckling and fracture. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b047-v13-26","title":"擬靜態反覆載重試驗：定量估算","titleEn":"Quasi-static cyclic column testing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「反覆載重遲滯迴圈」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cyclic hysteresis loops” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：1/2.5 縮尺試體柱高 4 m，最大水平力出現在漂移比 1.5%，強度下降到最大值 80% 時漂移比 5.0%，即極限位移 Δ_u = 0.05×4 = 0.20 m；降伏漂移比 0.9%（Δ_y = 0.036 m），位移韌性 μ = 0.20/0.036 ≈ 5.6。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A 1/2.5-scale specimen 4 m tall reaches peak lateral force at 1.5% drift and falls to 80% of peak at 5.0% drift, so ultimate displacement Δ_u = 0.05×4 = 0.20 m; with 0.9% yield drift (Δ_y = 0.036 m), displacement ductility μ = 0.20/0.036 ≈ 5.6. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：試驗計畫寫明軸力比、加載歷程、每級圈數、量測項目（柱頂位移、柱底曲率、鋼筋應變）與破壞定義（例如強度降至最大值 80%）；把試驗結果與彎矩—曲率加塑鉸長度的預測比較，誤差在可解釋範圍內才用於設計校驗。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: The test plan states axial-load ratio, loading history, cycles per step, measurements (top displacement, base curvature, bar strains) and the failure definition, for example strength falling to 80% of peak; compare results with the moment–curvature-plus-hinge-length prediction and use them for calibration only if differences are explainable.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"1/2.5 縮尺試體柱高 4 m，最大水平力出現在漂移比 1.5%，強度下降到最大值 80% 時漂移比 5.0%，即極限位移 Δ_u = 0.05×4 = 0.20 m；降伏漂移比 0.9%（Δ_y = 0.036 m），位移韌性 μ = 0.20/0.036 ≈ 5.6。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"A 1/2.5-scale specimen 4 m tall reaches peak lateral force at 1.5% drift and falls to 80% of peak at 5.0% drift, so ultimate displacement Δ_u = 0.05×4 = 0.20 m; with 0.9% yield drift (Δ_y = 0.036 m), displacement ductility μ = 0.20/0.036 ≈ 5.6. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「擬靜態反覆載重試驗」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Quasi-static cyclic column testing\", which statement holds?","options":["混凝土剪力強度是固定值，不會因柱子的彎曲變形而改變。","只要強度需求以韌性折減後滿足，就不必檢查位移。","1/2.5 縮尺試體柱高 4 m，最大水平力出現在漂移比 1.5%，強度下降到最大值 80% 時漂移比 5.0%，即極限位移 Δ_u = 0.05×4 = 0.20 m。"],"optionsEn":["The concrete shear strength is a fixed value that does not change with column flexural deformation.","If strength demand reduced by ductility is satisfied, displacement need not be checked.","A 1/2.5-scale specimen 4 m tall reaches peak lateral force at 1.5% drift and falls to 80% of peak at 5.0% drift, so ultimate displacement Δ_u = 0.05×4 = 0.20 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"1/2.5 縮尺試體柱高 4 m，最大水平力出現在漂移比 1.5%，強度下降到最大值 80% 時漂移比 5.0%，即極限位移 Δ_u = 0.05×4 = 0.20 m；降伏漂移比 0.9%（Δ_y = 0.036 m），位移韌性 μ = 0.20/0.036 ≈ 5.6。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A 1/2.5-scale specimen 4 m tall reaches peak lateral force at 1.5% drift and falls to 80% of peak at 5.0% drift, so ultimate displacement Δ_u = 0.05×4 = 0.20 m; with 0.9% yield drift (Δ_y = 0.036 m), displacement ductility μ = 0.20/0.036 ≈ 5.6. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b047-v13-27","title":"擬靜態反覆載重試驗：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Quasi-static cyclic column testing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「反覆載重遲滯迴圈」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cyclic hysteresis loops” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"試驗計畫寫明軸力比、加載歷程、每級圈數、量測項目（柱頂位移、柱底曲率、鋼筋應變）與破壞定義（例如強度降至最大值 80%）；把試驗結果與彎矩—曲率加塑鉸長度的預測比較，誤差在可解釋範圍內才用於設計校驗。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"The test plan states axial-load ratio, loading history, cycles per step, measurements (top displacement, base curvature, bar strains) and the failure definition, for example strength falling to 80% of peak; compare results with the moment–curvature-plus-hinge-length prediction and use them for calibration only if differences are explainable. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：引用試驗資料庫校驗設計時，要篩選軸力比、剪跨比、配筋率與本案相近的試體，並在報告中列出所選試體與篩選條件，避免以不相干的試驗支持設計假設。","observationEn":"Site practice: When calibrating against a test database, select specimens with axial-load ratio, shear-span ratio and reinforcement ratios close to the project and list the selection and criteria in the report, so unrelated tests are not used to support design assumptions.","failure":"注意干擾：只做單調推覆或圈數太少的試驗，會高估韌性；試體縮尺後若沒有同比例縮小箍筋與粒料，圍束與握裹行為與原型不同，試驗得到的漂移容量可能偏樂觀。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Monotonic pushover tests or too few cycles overestimate ductility; if hoops and aggregate are not scaled with the specimen, confinement and bond differ from the prototype and the measured drift capacity may be optimistic. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"試驗計畫寫明軸力比、加載歷程、每級圈數、量測項目（柱頂位移、柱底曲率、鋼筋應變）與破壞定義（例如強度降至最大值 80%）；把試驗結果與彎矩—曲率加塑鉸長度的預測比較，誤差在可解釋範圍內才用於設計校驗。","textEn":"The test plan states axial-load ratio, loading history, cycles per step, measurements (top displacement, base curvature, bar strains) and the failure definition, for example strength falling to 80% of peak; compare results with the moment–curvature-plus-hinge-length prediction and use them for calibration only if differences are explainable.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"引用試驗資料庫校驗設計時，要篩選軸力比、剪跨比、配筋率與本案相近的試體，並在報告中列出所選試體與篩選條件，避免以不相干的試驗支持設計假設。","textEn":"When calibrating against a test database, select specimens with axial-load ratio, shear-span ratio and reinforcement ratios close to the project and list the selection and criteria in the report, so unrelated tests are not used to support design assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「擬靜態反覆載重試驗」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Quasi-static cyclic column testing\"?","options":["試驗計畫寫明軸力比、加載歷程、每級圈數、量測項目（柱頂位移、柱底曲率、鋼筋應變）與破壞定義（例如強度降至最大值 80%）。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","塑鉸長度就是柱底出現裂縫的長度，可以在現場直接量到。"],"optionsEn":["The test plan states axial-load ratio, loading history, cycles per step, measurements (top displacement, base curvature, bar strains) and the failure definition, for example strength falling to 80% of peak.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","The plastic-hinge length is simply the cracked length at the column base and can be measured on site."],"answer":0,"explanation":"試驗計畫寫明軸力比、加載歷程、每級圈數、量測項目（柱頂位移、柱底曲率、鋼筋應變）與破壞定義（例如強度降至最大值 80%）；把試驗結果與彎矩—曲率加塑鉸長度的預測比較，誤差在可解釋範圍內才用於設計校驗。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"The test plan states axial-load ratio, loading history, cycles per step, measurements (top displacement, base curvature, bar strains) and the failure definition, for example strength falling to 80% of peak; compare results with the moment–curvature-plus-hinge-length prediction and use them for calibration only if differences are explainable. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b047-v13-28","title":"擬靜態反覆載重試驗：失效診斷","titleEn":"Quasi-static cyclic column testing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「反覆載重遲滯迴圈」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cyclic hysteresis loops” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只做單調推覆或圈數太少的試驗，會高估韌性；試體縮尺後若沒有同比例縮小箍筋與粒料，圍束與握裹行為與原型不同，試驗得到的漂移容量可能偏樂觀。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Monotonic pushover tests or too few cycles overestimate ductility; if hoops and aggregate are not scaled with the specimen, confinement and bond differ from the prototype and the measured drift capacity may be optimistic. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：試驗的用途是校驗分析模型與破壞準則，而不是證明單一設計。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Tests calibrate analysis models and failure criteria rather than proving a single design.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「單調推到破壞的試驗就足以代表地震下的柱韌性。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A monotonic push to failure is enough to represent column ductility under earthquakes.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只做單調推覆或圈數太少的試驗，會高估韌性；試體縮尺後若沒有同比例縮小箍筋與粒料，圍束與握裹行為與原型不同，試驗得到的漂移容量可能偏樂觀。","textEn":"Monotonic pushover tests or too few cycles overestimate ductility; if hoops and aggregate are not scaled with the specimen, confinement and bond differ from the prototype and the measured drift capacity may be optimistic.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「擬靜態反覆載重試驗」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Quasi-static cyclic column testing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","只做單調推覆或圈數太少的試驗，會高估韌性；試體縮尺後若沒有同比例縮小箍筋與粒料，圍束與握裹行為與原型不同，試驗得到的漂移容量可能偏樂觀。","震後柱子沒有倒，就表示可以直接恢復通行。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Monotonic pushover tests or too few cycles overestimate ductility.","If a column did not collapse in the earthquake, the bridge can reopen immediately."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只做單調推覆或圈數太少的試驗，會高估韌性；試體縮尺後若沒有同比例縮小箍筋與粒料，圍束與握裹行為與原型不同，試驗得到的漂移容量可能偏樂觀。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Monotonic pushover tests or too few cycles overestimate ductility; if hoops and aggregate are not scaled with the specimen, confinement and bond differ from the prototype and the measured drift capacity may be optimistic. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b047-v13-29","title":"震後損傷量測與殘留變形：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Post-earthquake damage measurement and residual deformation: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「殘留漂移比」如何影響橋墩塑鉸韌性設計的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Residual drift ratio” governs force, deformation or durability in “Ductile plastic-hinge design for bridge piers”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"韌性設計允許塑鉸損傷，因此震後要能快速判斷橋墩還能不能用：可觀察的指標包括裂縫寬度、保護層剝落範圍、主筋外露或挫屈，以及柱的殘留傾斜。殘留漂移比是決定能否修復的關鍵，因為傾斜的柱在重力下產生 P-Δ 二次彎矩，降低後續地震的安全餘裕；1995 年阪神地震後日本在設計中引入殘留位移檢核，即是為了避免大量傾斜橋墩只能拆除重建。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「殘留漂移比」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Ductile design accepts hinge damage, so after an earthquake engineers must judge quickly whether a pier can stay in service: observable indicators include crack width, extent of cover spalling, exposed or buckled bars and the column's residual tilt. Residual drift is the key repairability criterion because a tilted column carries second-order P-Δ moment under gravity, eroding safety for later earthquakes; after the 1995 Kobe earthquake Japan introduced residual-displacement checks into design to avoid large numbers of tilted piers that could only be demolished and rebuilt. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Residual drift ratio” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：殘留漂移比 = Δ_r/H = 0.08/10 = 0.8%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Residual drift = Δ_r/H = 0.08/10 = 0.8%.","failure":"常見誤解：「震後柱子沒有倒，就表示可以直接恢復通行。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If a column did not collapse in the earthquake, the bridge can reopen immediately.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「殘留漂移比」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Residual drift ratio”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-29-k1","title":"震後損傷量測與殘留變形","titleEn":"Post-earthquake damage measurement and residual deformation","text":"韌性設計允許塑鉸損傷，因此震後要能快速判斷橋墩還能不能用：可觀察的指標包括裂縫寬度、保護層剝落範圍、主筋外露或挫屈，以及柱的殘留傾斜。殘留漂移比是決定能否修復的關鍵，因為傾斜的柱在重力下產生 P-Δ 二次彎矩，降低後續地震的安全餘裕；1995 年阪神地震後日本在設計中引入殘留位移檢核，即是為了避免大量傾斜橋墩只能拆除重建。","textEn":"Ductile design accepts hinge damage, so after an earthquake engineers must judge quickly whether a pier can stay in service: observable indicators include crack width, extent of cover spalling, exposed or buckled bars and the column's residual tilt. Residual drift is the key repairability criterion because a tilted column carries second-order P-Δ moment under gravity, eroding safety for later earthquakes; after the 1995 Kobe earthquake Japan introduced residual-displacement checks into design to avoid large numbers of tilted piers that could only be demolished and rebuilt.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：震後柱子沒有倒，就表示可以直接恢復通行。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If a column did not collapse in the earthquake, the bridge can reopen immediately. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「震後損傷量測與殘留變形」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Post-earthquake damage measurement and residual deformation\" is correct?","options":["震後柱子沒有倒，就表示可以直接恢復通行。","耐震與耐久是兩個獨立問題，腐蝕不會影響橋墩的耐震能力。","韌性設計允許塑鉸損傷，因此震後要能快速判斷橋墩還能不能用：可觀察的指標包括裂縫寬度、保護層剝落範圍、主筋外露或挫屈，以及柱的殘留傾斜。"],"optionsEn":["If a column did not collapse in the earthquake, the bridge can reopen immediately.","Seismic and durability performance are separate issues; corrosion does not affect a pier's seismic capacity.","Ductile design accepts hinge damage, so after an earthquake engineers must judge quickly whether a pier can stay in service: observable indicators include crack width, extent of cover spalling, exposed or buckled bars and the column's residual tilt."],"answer":2,"explanation":"韌性設計允許塑鉸損傷，因此震後要能快速判斷橋墩還能不能用：可觀察的指標包括裂縫寬度、保護層剝落範圍、主筋外露或挫屈，以及柱的殘留傾斜。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Ductile design accepts hinge damage, so after an earthquake engineers must judge quickly whether a pier can stay in service: observable indicators include crack width, extent of cover spalling, exposed or buckled bars and the column's residual tilt. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b047-v13-30","title":"震後損傷量測與殘留變形：定量估算","titleEn":"Post-earthquake damage measurement and residual deformation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「殘留漂移比」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Residual drift ratio” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：殘留漂移比 = Δ_r/H = 0.08/10 = 0.8%。P-Δ 二次彎矩 = P·Δ_r = 8 MN×0.08 m = 0.64 MN·m，約為 M_p = 12 MN·m 的 5.3%，低於設計時常用的 20% 檢核比例；若 Δ_r = 0.30 m，P-Δ 為 2.4 MN·m，即達 20%。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Residual drift = Δ_r/H = 0.08/10 = 0.8%. The P-Δ moment = P·Δ_r = 8 MN×0.08 m = 0.64 MN·m, about 5.3% of M_p = 12 MN·m, below the 20% ratio commonly checked in design; a residual of 0.30 m gives 2.4 MN·m, reaching 20%. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：震後以全站儀或傾斜儀量測柱頂相對柱底的水平偏移，記錄裂縫寬度、剝落高度與主筋狀態，並與設計時預估的損傷等級比較；超過門檻（例如殘留漂移 1%，教學假設）或主筋挫屈時，限制通行並由結構工程師評估。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: After an earthquake measure the horizontal offset of column top relative to base with a total station or inclinometer, record crack widths, spalling height and bar condition, and compare with the damage state predicted at design; beyond a threshold, for example 1% residual drift as a teaching assumption, or with buckled bars, restrict traffic pending a structural engineer's assessment.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"殘留漂移比 = Δ_r/H = 0.08/10 = 0.8%。P-Δ 二次彎矩 = P·Δ_r = 8 MN×0.08 m = 0.64 MN·m，約為 M_p = 12 MN·m 的 5.3%，低於設計時常用的 20% 檢核比例；若 Δ_r = 0.30 m，P-Δ 為 2.4 MN·m，即達 20%。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Residual drift = Δ_r/H = 0.08/10 = 0.8%. The P-Δ moment = P·Δ_r = 8 MN×0.08 m = 0.64 MN·m, about 5.3% of M_p = 12 MN·m, below the 20% ratio commonly checked in design; a residual of 0.30 m gives 2.4 MN·m, reaching 20%. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「震後損傷量測與殘留變形」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Post-earthquake damage measurement and residual deformation\", which statement holds?","options":["殘留漂移比 = Δ_r/H = 0.08/10 = 0.8%。","橋墩越強越好，所有構件都加強就能確保耐震安全。","箍筋主要是用來固定主筋位置，對耐震性能影響不大。"],"optionsEn":["Residual drift = Δ_r/H = 0.08/10 = 0.8%.","The stronger the pier the better; strengthening every member guarantees seismic safety.","Hoops mainly hold the longitudinal bars in place and matter little for seismic performance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"殘留漂移比 = Δ_r/H = 0.08/10 = 0.8%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Residual drift = Δ_r/H = 0.08/10 = 0.8%. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b047-v13-31","title":"震後損傷量測與殘留變形：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Post-earthquake damage measurement and residual deformation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「殘留漂移比」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Residual drift ratio” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"震後以全站儀或傾斜儀量測柱頂相對柱底的水平偏移，記錄裂縫寬度、剝落高度與主筋狀態，並與設計時預估的損傷等級比較；超過門檻（例如殘留漂移 1%，教學假設）或主筋挫屈時，限制通行並由結構工程師評估。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"After an earthquake measure the horizontal offset of column top relative to base with a total station or inclinometer, record crack widths, spalling height and bar condition, and compare with the damage state predicted at design; beyond a threshold, for example 1% residual drift as a teaching assumption, or with buckled bars, restrict traffic pending a structural engineer's assessment. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：震後檢查程序要事先分級（立即通行、限制通行、封閉），每級對應裂縫、剝落、殘留漂移與主筋狀態的量化門檻；量測基準點與柱的竣工垂直度在交接時就要建立。","observationEn":"Site practice: Grade the post-earthquake procedure in advance into open, restricted and closed, each tied to quantitative thresholds for cracking, spalling, residual drift and bar condition; set up survey reference points and as-built column plumbness at handover.","failure":"注意干擾：未量測殘留傾斜就恢復通行，若主筋已挫屈或柱核心已壓碎，餘震中柱可能失去軸向承載；1995 年阪神地震中阪神高速神戶線有多處高架段整段側倒，正顯示缺乏韌性與殘留變形控制的後果。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Reopening without measuring residual tilt risks loss of axial capacity in aftershocks if bars have buckled or the core has crushed; in the 1995 Kobe earthquake several elevated sections of the Hanshin Expressway Kobe Route toppled sideways, showing the consequence of lacking ductility and residual-deformation control. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"震後以全站儀或傾斜儀量測柱頂相對柱底的水平偏移，記錄裂縫寬度、剝落高度與主筋狀態，並與設計時預估的損傷等級比較；超過門檻（例如殘留漂移 1%，教學假設）或主筋挫屈時，限制通行並由結構工程師評估。","textEn":"After an earthquake measure the horizontal offset of column top relative to base with a total station or inclinometer, record crack widths, spalling height and bar condition, and compare with the damage state predicted at design; beyond a threshold, for example 1% residual drift as a teaching assumption, or with buckled bars, restrict traffic pending a structural engineer's assessment.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"震後檢查程序要事先分級（立即通行、限制通行、封閉），每級對應裂縫、剝落、殘留漂移與主筋狀態的量化門檻；量測基準點與柱的竣工垂直度在交接時就要建立。","textEn":"Grade the post-earthquake procedure in advance into open, restricted and closed, each tied to quantitative thresholds for cracking, spalling, residual drift and bar condition; set up survey reference points and as-built column plumbness at handover.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「震後損傷量測與殘留變形」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Post-earthquake damage measurement and residual deformation\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","震後以全站儀或傾斜儀量測柱頂相對柱底的水平偏移，記錄裂縫寬度、剝落高度與主筋狀態，並與設計時預估的損傷等級比較。","箍筋間距差幾公分不影響結構安全，可以依現場方便調整。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","After an earthquake measure the horizontal offset of column top relative to base with a total station or inclinometer, record crack widths, spalling height and bar condition, and compare with the damage state predicted at design.","A few centimetres of extra hoop spacing do not affect safety and can be adjusted for site convenience."],"answer":1,"explanation":"震後以全站儀或傾斜儀量測柱頂相對柱底的水平偏移，記錄裂縫寬度、剝落高度與主筋狀態，並與設計時預估的損傷等級比較；超過門檻（例如殘留漂移 1%，教學假設）或主筋挫屈時，限制通行並由結構工程師評估。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"After an earthquake measure the horizontal offset of column top relative to base with a total station or inclinometer, record crack widths, spalling height and bar condition, and compare with the damage state predicted at design; beyond a threshold, for example 1% residual drift as a teaching assumption, or with buckled bars, restrict traffic pending a structural engineer's assessment. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b047-v13-32","title":"震後損傷量測與殘留變形：失效診斷","titleEn":"Post-earthquake damage measurement and residual deformation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「殘留漂移比」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Residual drift ratio” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"未量測殘留傾斜就恢復通行，若主筋已挫屈或柱核心已壓碎，餘震中柱可能失去軸向承載；1995 年阪神地震中阪神高速神戶線有多處高架段整段側倒，正顯示缺乏韌性與殘留變形控制的後果。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Reopening without measuring residual tilt risks loss of axial capacity in aftershocks if bars have buckled or the core has crushed; in the 1995 Kobe earthquake several elevated sections of the Hanshin Expressway Kobe Route toppled sideways, showing the consequence of lacking ductility and residual-deformation control. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：殘留漂移比是決定能否修復的關鍵，因為傾斜的柱在重力下產生 P-Δ 二次彎矩，降低後續地震的安全餘裕；1995 年阪神地震後日本在設計中引入殘留位移檢核，即是為了避免大量傾斜橋墩只能拆除重建。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Residual drift is the key repairability criterion because a tilted column carries second-order P-Δ moment under gravity, eroding safety for later earthquakes; after the 1995 Kobe earthquake Japan introduced residual-displacement checks into design to avoid large numbers of tilted piers that could only be demolished and rebuilt.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「震後柱子沒有倒，就表示可以直接恢復通行。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If a column did not collapse in the earthquake, the bridge can reopen immediately.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"未量測殘留傾斜就恢復通行，若主筋已挫屈或柱核心已壓碎，餘震中柱可能失去軸向承載；1995 年阪神地震中阪神高速神戶線有多處高架段整段側倒，正顯示缺乏韌性與殘留變形控制的後果。","textEn":"Reopening without measuring residual tilt risks loss of axial capacity in aftershocks if bars have buckled or the core has crushed; in the 1995 Kobe earthquake several elevated sections of the Hanshin Expressway Kobe Route toppled sideways, showing the consequence of lacking ductility and residual-deformation control.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「震後損傷量測與殘留變形」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Post-earthquake damage measurement and residual deformation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","耐震與耐久是兩個獨立問題，腐蝕不會影響橋墩的耐震能力。","未量測殘留傾斜就恢復通行，若主筋已挫屈或柱核心已壓碎，餘震中柱可能失去軸向承載。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Seismic and durability performance are separate issues; corrosion does not affect a pier's seismic capacity.","Reopening without measuring residual tilt risks loss of axial capacity in aftershocks if bars have buckled or the core has crushed."],"answer":2,"explanation":"未量測殘留傾斜就恢復通行，若主筋已挫屈或柱核心已壓碎，餘震中柱可能失去軸向承載；1995 年阪神地震中阪神高速神戶線有多處高架段整段側倒，正顯示缺乏韌性與殘留變形控制的後果。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Reopening without measuring residual tilt risks loss of axial capacity in aftershocks if bars have buckled or the core has crushed; in the 1995 Kobe earthquake several elevated sections of the Hanshin Expressway Kobe Route toppled sideways, showing the consequence of lacking ductility and residual-deformation control. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b047-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「塑鉸區的耐久性與箍筋腐蝕」與「既有橋墩評估與工程交接」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Durability of the hinge zone and hoop corrosion\" and \"Assessing existing piers and engineering handover\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b047-v13-33","title":"塑鉸區的耐久性與箍筋腐蝕：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Durability of the hinge zone and hoop corrosion: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「塑鉸區保護層」如何影響橋墩塑鉸韌性設計的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Hinge-zone cover” governs force, deformation or durability in “Ductile plastic-hinge design for bridge piers”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"柱底塑鉸區通常在地面或水面附近，最容易受到乾濕循環、鹽分、除冰鹽或河水沖刷磨耗；箍筋位於最外層，比主筋更早腐蝕。箍筋斷面一旦因腐蝕減少，圍束能力與剪力強度同步下降，而這兩者正是韌性設計賴以成立的條件。因此耐久設計（保護層厚度、混凝土品質、裂縫控制、表面保護）在塑鉸區不只是延壽問題，而是維持耐震性能的必要條件。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「塑鉸區保護層」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The base hinge zone usually sits near ground or water level, where it is most exposed to wetting and drying, salts, de-icing salts and abrasion by river flow; hoops lie outermost and corrode before longitudinal bars. Once corrosion reduces hoop area, confinement and shear strength fall together, and those are exactly the conditions ductile design relies on. Durability design (cover, concrete quality, crack control and surface protection) in the hinge zone is therefore not just about service life but a prerequisite for keeping seismic performance. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Hinge-zone cover” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：箍筋腐蝕使有效面積減少 20%，ρ_s 由 0.0080 降為 0.0064，ε_cu = 0.004 + 1.4×0.0064×475×0.09/50 ≈ 0.0117，比原設計 0.0136 低約 14%，塑鉸轉角容量也相應降低。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Corrosion that removes 20% of hoop area lowers ρ_s from 0.0080 to 0.0064, so ε_cu = 0.004 + 1.4×0.0064×475×0.09/50 ≈ 0.0117, about 14% below the original 0.0136, with a corresponding loss of hinge rotation capacity.","failure":"常見誤解：「耐震與耐久是兩個獨立問題，腐蝕不會影響橋墩的耐震能力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Seismic and durability performance are separate issues; corrosion does not affect a pier's seismic capacity.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「塑鉸區保護層」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Hinge-zone cover”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-33-k1","title":"塑鉸區的耐久性與箍筋腐蝕","titleEn":"Durability of the hinge zone and hoop corrosion","text":"柱底塑鉸區通常在地面或水面附近，最容易受到乾濕循環、鹽分、除冰鹽或河水沖刷磨耗；箍筋位於最外層，比主筋更早腐蝕。箍筋斷面一旦因腐蝕減少，圍束能力與剪力強度同步下降，而這兩者正是韌性設計賴以成立的條件。","textEn":"The base hinge zone usually sits near ground or water level, where it is most exposed to wetting and drying, salts, de-icing salts and abrasion by river flow; hoops lie outermost and corrode before longitudinal bars. Once corrosion reduces hoop area, confinement and shear strength fall together, and those are exactly the conditions ductile design relies on.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：耐震與耐久是兩個獨立問題，腐蝕不會影響橋墩的耐震能力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Seismic and durability performance are separate issues; corrosion does not affect a pier's seismic capacity. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「塑鉸區的耐久性與箍筋腐蝕」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Durability of the hinge zone and hoop corrosion\" is correct?","options":["柱底塑鉸區通常在地面或水面附近，最容易受到乾濕循環、鹽分、除冰鹽或河水沖刷磨耗；箍筋位於最外層，比主筋更早腐蝕。","耐震與耐久是兩個獨立問題，腐蝕不會影響橋墩的耐震能力。","混凝土剪力強度是固定值，不會因柱子的彎曲變形而改變。"],"optionsEn":["The base hinge zone usually sits near ground or water level, where it is most exposed to wetting and drying, salts, de-icing salts and abrasion by river flow.","Seismic and durability performance are separate issues; corrosion does not affect a pier's seismic capacity.","The concrete shear strength is a fixed value that does not change with column flexural deformation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"柱底塑鉸區通常在地面或水面附近，最容易受到乾濕循環、鹽分、除冰鹽或河水沖刷磨耗；箍筋位於最外層，比主筋更早腐蝕。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The base hinge zone usually sits near ground or water level, where it is most exposed to wetting and drying, salts, de-icing salts and abrasion by river flow; hoops lie outermost and corrode before longitudinal bars. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b047-v13-34","title":"塑鉸區的耐久性與箍筋腐蝕：定量估算","titleEn":"Durability of the hinge zone and hoop corrosion: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「塑鉸區保護層」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Hinge-zone cover” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：箍筋腐蝕使有效面積減少 20%，ρ_s 由 0.0080 降為 0.0064，ε_cu = 0.004 + 1.4×0.0064×475×0.09/50 ≈ 0.0117，比原設計 0.0136 低約 14%，塑鉸轉角容量也相應降低。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Corrosion that removes 20% of hoop area lowers ρ_s from 0.0080 to 0.0064, so ε_cu = 0.004 + 1.4×0.0064×475×0.09/50 ≈ 0.0117, about 14% below the original 0.0136, with a corresponding loss of hinge rotation capacity. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：定期檢查柱底的鏽水、裂縫與剝落，必要時以保護層厚度計、半電池電位與氯離子含量取樣評估腐蝕風險；發現箍筋外露時量測殘餘直徑，回算圍束與剪力強度並與原設計比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Inspect column bases periodically for rust staining, cracking and spalling, and where needed assess corrosion risk with cover meters, half-cell potential and chloride sampling; where hoops are exposed, measure remaining diameter and back-calculate confinement and shear strength against the original design.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"箍筋腐蝕使有效面積減少 20%，ρ_s 由 0.0080 降為 0.0064，ε_cu = 0.004 + 1.4×0.0064×475×0.09/50 ≈ 0.0117，比原設計 0.0136 低約 14%，塑鉸轉角容量也相應降低。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Corrosion that removes 20% of hoop area lowers ρ_s from 0.0080 to 0.0064, so ε_cu = 0.004 + 1.4×0.0064×475×0.09/50 ≈ 0.0117, about 14% below the original 0.0136, with a corresponding loss of hinge rotation capacity. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「塑鉸區的耐久性與箍筋腐蝕」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Durability of the hinge zone and hoop corrosion\", which statement holds?","options":["只要強度需求以韌性折減後滿足，就不必檢查位移。","箍筋腐蝕使有效面積減少 20%，ρ_s 由 0.0080 降為 0.0064，ε_cu = 0.004 + 1.4×0.0064×475×0.09/50 ≈ 0.0117，比原設計 0.0136 低約 14%，塑鉸轉角容量也相應降低。","塑鉸長度就是柱底出現裂縫的長度，可以在現場直接量到。"],"optionsEn":["If strength demand reduced by ductility is satisfied, displacement need not be checked.","Corrosion that removes 20% of hoop area lowers ρ_s from 0.0080 to 0.0064, so ε_cu = 0.004 + 1.4×0.0064×475×0.09/50 ≈ 0.0117, about 14% below the original 0.0136, with a corresponding loss of hinge rotation capacity.","The plastic-hinge length is simply the cracked length at the column base and can be measured on site."],"answer":1,"explanation":"箍筋腐蝕使有效面積減少 20%，ρ_s 由 0.0080 降為 0.0064，ε_cu = 0.004 + 1.4×0.0064×475×0.09/50 ≈ 0.0117，比原設計 0.0136 低約 14%，塑鉸轉角容量也相應降低。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Corrosion that removes 20% of hoop area lowers ρ_s from 0.0080 to 0.0064, so ε_cu = 0.004 + 1.4×0.0064×475×0.09/50 ≈ 0.0117, about 14% below the original 0.0136, with a corresponding loss of hinge rotation capacity. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b047-v13-35","title":"塑鉸區的耐久性與箍筋腐蝕：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Durability of the hinge zone and hoop corrosion: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「塑鉸區保護層」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Hinge-zone cover” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"定期檢查柱底的鏽水、裂縫與剝落，必要時以保護層厚度計、半電池電位與氯離子含量取樣評估腐蝕風險；發現箍筋外露時量測殘餘直徑，回算圍束與剪力強度並與原設計比較。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Inspect column bases periodically for rust staining, cracking and spalling, and where needed assess corrosion risk with cover meters, half-cell potential and chloride sampling; where hoops are exposed, measure remaining diameter and back-calculate confinement and shear strength against the original design. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：塑鉸區保護層厚度、混凝土等級與表面保護要依暴露環境提高，河中橋墩加設防撞與防磨耗保護；檢查手冊把柱底箍筋狀態列為耐震關鍵項目，並設定修復門檻。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase hinge-zone cover, concrete grade and surface protection to suit exposure, and add impact and abrasion protection for in-river piers; the inspection manual lists base hoop condition as a seismic-critical item with defined repair thresholds.","failure":"注意干擾：河川或沿海橋墩柱底保護層被沖刷磨耗、箍筋鏽斷，平時外觀只是局部剝落，地震時塑鉸區卻提早剪力破壞或主筋挫屈，原本設計的韌性容量已不存在。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: At river or coastal piers, abraded cover and corroded-through hoops at the column base look like minor spalling in service, yet in an earthquake the hinge zone fails early in shear or by bar buckling, because the designed ductility capacity no longer exists. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"定期檢查柱底的鏽水、裂縫與剝落，必要時以保護層厚度計、半電池電位與氯離子含量取樣評估腐蝕風險；發現箍筋外露時量測殘餘直徑，回算圍束與剪力強度並與原設計比較。","textEn":"Inspect column bases periodically for rust staining, cracking and spalling, and where needed assess corrosion risk with cover meters, half-cell potential and chloride sampling; where hoops are exposed, measure remaining diameter and back-calculate confinement and shear strength against the original design.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"塑鉸區保護層厚度、混凝土等級與表面保護要依暴露環境提高，河中橋墩加設防撞與防磨耗保護；檢查手冊把柱底箍筋狀態列為耐震關鍵項目，並設定修復門檻。","textEn":"Increase hinge-zone cover, concrete grade and surface protection to suit exposure, and add impact and abrasion protection for in-river piers; the inspection manual lists base hoop condition as a seismic-critical item with defined repair thresholds.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「塑鉸區的耐久性與箍筋腐蝕」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Durability of the hinge zone and hoop corrosion\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","只要續接器能承受鋼筋的降伏強度，就可以用在塑鉸區。","定期檢查柱底的鏽水、裂縫與剝落，必要時以保護層厚度計、半電池電位與氯離子含量取樣評估腐蝕風險；發現箍筋外露時量測殘餘直徑，回算圍束與剪力強度並與原設計比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Any coupler that develops the bar's yield strength can be used in a plastic hinge zone.","Inspect column bases periodically for rust staining, cracking and spalling, and where needed assess corrosion risk with cover meters, half-cell potential and chloride sampling."],"answer":2,"explanation":"定期檢查柱底的鏽水、裂縫與剝落，必要時以保護層厚度計、半電池電位與氯離子含量取樣評估腐蝕風險；發現箍筋外露時量測殘餘直徑，回算圍束與剪力強度並與原設計比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Inspect column bases periodically for rust staining, cracking and spalling, and where needed assess corrosion risk with cover meters, half-cell potential and chloride sampling; where hoops are exposed, measure remaining diameter and back-calculate confinement and shear strength against the original design. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b047-v13-36","title":"塑鉸區的耐久性與箍筋腐蝕：失效診斷","titleEn":"Durability of the hinge zone and hoop corrosion: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「塑鉸區保護層」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Hinge-zone cover” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"河川或沿海橋墩柱底保護層被沖刷磨耗、箍筋鏽斷，平時外觀只是局部剝落，地震時塑鉸區卻提早剪力破壞或主筋挫屈，原本設計的韌性容量已不存在。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"At river or coastal piers, abraded cover and corroded-through hoops at the column base look like minor spalling in service, yet in an earthquake the hinge zone fails early in shear or by bar buckling, because the designed ductility capacity no longer exists. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：因此耐久設計（保護層厚度、混凝土品質、裂縫控制、表面保護）在塑鉸區不只是延壽問題，而是維持耐震性能的必要條件。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Durability design (cover, concrete quality, crack control and surface protection) in the hinge zone is therefore not just about service life but a prerequisite for keeping seismic performance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「耐震與耐久是兩個獨立問題，腐蝕不會影響橋墩的耐震能力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Seismic and durability performance are separate issues; corrosion does not affect a pier's seismic capacity.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"河川或沿海橋墩柱底保護層被沖刷磨耗、箍筋鏽斷，平時外觀只是局部剝落，地震時塑鉸區卻提早剪力破壞或主筋挫屈，原本設計的韌性容量已不存在。","textEn":"At river or coastal piers, abraded cover and corroded-through hoops at the column base look like minor spalling in service, yet in an earthquake the hinge zone fails early in shear or by bar buckling, because the designed ductility capacity no longer exists.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「塑鉸區的耐久性與箍筋腐蝕」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Durability of the hinge zone and hoop corrosion\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["河川或沿海橋墩柱底保護層被沖刷磨耗、箍筋鏽斷，平時外觀只是局部剝落，地震時塑鉸區卻提早剪力破壞或主筋挫屈，原本設計的韌性容量已不存在。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","混凝土剪力強度是固定值，不會因柱子的彎曲變形而改變。"],"optionsEn":["At river or coastal piers, abraded cover and corroded-through hoops at the column base look like minor spalling in service, yet in an earthquake the hinge zone fails early in shear or by bar buckling, because the designed ductility capacity no longer exists.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","The concrete shear strength is a fixed value that does not change with column flexural deformation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"河川或沿海橋墩柱底保護層被沖刷磨耗、箍筋鏽斷，平時外觀只是局部剝落，地震時塑鉸區卻提早剪力破壞或主筋挫屈，原本設計的韌性容量已不存在。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"At river or coastal piers, abraded cover and corroded-through hoops at the column base look like minor spalling in service, yet in an earthquake the hinge zone fails early in shear or by bar buckling, because the designed ductility capacity no longer exists. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b047-v13-37","title":"既有橋墩評估與工程交接：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Assessing existing piers and engineering handover: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「剪力隨韌性退化」如何影響橋墩塑鉸韌性設計的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Shear degradation with ductility” governs force, deformation or durability in “Ductile plastic-hinge design for bridge piers”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"依舊規範設計的橋墩常見三種韌性缺陷：圍束箍筋太少、柱底主筋搭接、以及剪力強度不足。混凝土提供的剪力強度會隨塑鉸轉動而退化，因為斜裂縫張開、骨材互鎖減弱，所以即使柱在小變形時剪力足夠，進入韌性範圍後也可能剪斷，短柱尤其危險。評估流程是先求彎曲容量對應的剪力需求，再與隨韌性退化的剪力容量比較，判斷破壞模式；結果決定是否需要鋼板包覆或纖維複材補強，並寫入交接與維護文件。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「剪力隨韌性退化」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Piers designed to older codes commonly show three ductility deficiencies: too little confinement, lap splices at the column base and inadequate shear strength. The concrete contribution to shear degrades as the hinge rotates, because diagonal cracks open and aggregate interlock weakens, so a column with adequate shear at small deformation can fail in shear once it enters the ductile range, short columns especially. Assessment first finds the shear demand corresponding to flexural capacity, then compares it with shear capacity degrading with ductility to identify the failure mode; the result decides whether steel or fibre-reinforced-polymer jacketing is needed and is written into handover and maintenance records. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Shear degradation with ductility” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：V_c = k·√f′_c·A_e，f′_c = 30 MPa、A_e = 0.8×π×1.0² ≈ 2.51 m²：μ ≤ 2 時 k = 0.29，V_c ≈ 3.99 MN；μ = 4 時 k = 0.10，V_c ≈ 1.38 MN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: V_c = k·√f′_c·A_e with f′_c = 30 MPa and A_e = 0.8×π×1.0² ≈ 2.51 m²: k = 0.29 for μ ≤ 2 gives V_c ≈ 3.99 MN; k = 0.10 at μ = 4 gives V_c ≈ 1.38 MN.","failure":"常見誤解：「混凝土剪力強度是固定值，不會因柱子的彎曲變形而改變。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The concrete shear strength is a fixed value that does not change with column flexural deformation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「剪力隨韌性退化」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Shear degradation with ductility”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-37-k1","title":"既有橋墩評估與工程交接","titleEn":"Assessing existing piers and engineering handover","text":"依舊規範設計的橋墩常見三種韌性缺陷：圍束箍筋太少、柱底主筋搭接、以及剪力強度不足。混凝土提供的剪力強度會隨塑鉸轉動而退化，因為斜裂縫張開、骨材互鎖減弱，所以即使柱在小變形時剪力足夠，進入韌性範圍後也可能剪斷，短柱尤其危險。","textEn":"Piers designed to older codes commonly show three ductility deficiencies: too little confinement, lap splices at the column base and inadequate shear strength. The concrete contribution to shear degrades as the hinge rotates, because diagonal cracks open and aggregate interlock weakens, so a column with adequate shear at small deformation can fail in shear once it enters the ductile range, short columns especially.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：混凝土剪力強度是固定值，不會因柱子的彎曲變形而改變。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The concrete shear strength is a fixed value that does not change with column flexural deformation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「既有橋墩評估與工程交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Assessing existing piers and engineering handover\" is correct?","options":["混凝土剪力強度是固定值，不會因柱子的彎曲變形而改變。","依舊規範設計的橋墩常見三種韌性缺陷：圍束箍筋太少、柱底主筋搭接、以及剪力強度不足。","橋墩越強越好，所有構件都加強就能確保耐震安全。"],"optionsEn":["The concrete shear strength is a fixed value that does not change with column flexural deformation.","Piers designed to older codes commonly show three ductility deficiencies: too little confinement, lap splices at the column base and inadequate shear strength.","The stronger the pier the better; strengthening every member guarantees seismic safety."],"answer":1,"explanation":"依舊規範設計的橋墩常見三種韌性缺陷：圍束箍筋太少、柱底主筋搭接、以及剪力強度不足。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Piers designed to older codes commonly show three ductility deficiencies: too little confinement, lap splices at the column base and inadequate shear strength. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b047-v13-38","title":"既有橋墩評估與工程交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Assessing existing piers and engineering handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「剪力隨韌性退化」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Shear degradation with ductility” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：V_c = k·√f′_c·A_e，f′_c = 30 MPa、A_e = 0.8×π×1.0² ≈ 2.51 m²：μ ≤ 2 時 k = 0.29，V_c ≈ 3.99 MN；μ = 4 時 k = 0.10，V_c ≈ 1.38 MN。舊箍筋 13 mm@300 mm 提供 V_s ≈ 0.64 MN，合計 2.02 MN；6 m 短柱 V_o = 2.4 MN，判定韌性未達 4 即剪力破壞。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: V_c = k·√f′_c·A_e with f′_c = 30 MPa and A_e = 0.8×π×1.0² ≈ 2.51 m²: k = 0.29 for μ ≤ 2 gives V_c ≈ 3.99 MN; k = 0.10 at μ = 4 gives V_c ≈ 1.38 MN. Old 13 mm hoops at 300 mm add V_s ≈ 0.64 MN, 2.02 MN in total; a 6 m short column with V_o = 2.4 MN fails in shear before reaching μ = 4. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以竣工圖與現地取樣（鑽心強度、鋼筋掃描、局部打除確認箍筋與搭接）建立既有橋墩模型，進行推覆分析並同時繪出剪力需求與剪力容量隨位移的曲線，交點即破壞模式判斷依據；評估結果須經第二位工程師複核。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build the existing-pier model from as-built drawings and site sampling (core strengths, rebar scanning, local breakouts to confirm hoops and splices), run a pushover and plot shear demand and degrading shear capacity against displacement, using their intersection to identify the failure mode; a second engineer checks the assessment.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"V_c = k·√f′_c·A_e，f′_c = 30 MPa、A_e = 0.8×π×1.0² ≈ 2.51 m²：μ ≤ 2 時 k = 0.29，V_c ≈ 3.99 MN；μ = 4 時 k = 0.10，V_c ≈ 1.38 MN。舊箍筋 13 mm@300 mm 提供 V_s ≈ 0.64 MN，合計 2.02 MN；6 m 短柱 V_o = 2.4 MN，判定韌性未達 4 即剪力破壞。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"V_c = k·√f′_c·A_e with f′_c = 30 MPa and A_e = 0.8×π×1.0² ≈ 2.51 m²: k = 0.29 for μ ≤ 2 gives V_c ≈ 3.99 MN; k = 0.10 at μ = 4 gives V_c ≈ 1.38 MN. Old 13 mm hoops at 300 mm add V_s ≈ 0.64 MN, 2.02 MN in total; a 6 m short column with V_o = 2.4 MN fails in shear before reaching μ = 4. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「既有橋墩評估與工程交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Assessing existing piers and engineering handover\", which statement holds?","options":["箍筋主要是用來固定主筋位置，對耐震性能影響不大。","箍筋間距差幾公分不影響結構安全，可以依現場方便調整。","V_c = k·√f′_c·A_e，f′_c = 30 MPa、A_e = 0.8×π×1.0² ≈ 2.51 m²：μ ≤ 2 時 k = 0.29，V_c ≈ 3.99 MN。"],"optionsEn":["Hoops mainly hold the longitudinal bars in place and matter little for seismic performance.","A few centimetres of extra hoop spacing do not affect safety and can be adjusted for site convenience.","V_c = k·√f′_c·A_e with f′_c = 30 MPa and A_e = 0.8×π×1.0² ≈ 2.51 m²: k = 0.29 for μ ≤ 2 gives V_c ≈ 3.99 MN; k = 0.10 at μ = 4 gives V_c ≈ 1.38 MN."],"answer":2,"explanation":"V_c = k·√f′_c·A_e，f′_c = 30 MPa、A_e = 0.8×π×1.0² ≈ 2.51 m²：μ ≤ 2 時 k = 0.29，V_c ≈ 3.99 MN；μ = 4 時 k = 0.10，V_c ≈ 1.38 MN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"V_c = k·√f′_c·A_e with f′_c = 30 MPa and A_e = 0.8×π×1.0² ≈ 2.51 m²: k = 0.29 for μ ≤ 2 gives V_c ≈ 3.99 MN; k = 0.10 at μ = 4 gives V_c ≈ 1.38 MN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b047-v13-39","title":"既有橋墩評估與工程交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Assessing existing piers and engineering handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「剪力隨韌性退化」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Shear degradation with ductility” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以竣工圖與現地取樣（鑽心強度、鋼筋掃描、局部打除確認箍筋與搭接）建立既有橋墩模型，進行推覆分析並同時繪出剪力需求與剪力容量隨位移的曲線，交點即破壞模式判斷依據；評估結果須經第二位工程師複核。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build the existing-pier model from as-built drawings and site sampling (core strengths, rebar scanning, local breakouts to confirm hoops and splices), run a pushover and plot shear demand and degrading shear capacity against displacement, using their intersection to identify the failure mode; a second engineer checks the assessment. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接文件應包含每座排架的推覆曲線、破壞模式判斷、塑鉸區配筋竣工照片、續接器試驗報告與震後檢查門檻；既有橋墩評估若顯示剪力先於彎曲破壞，須排入補強計畫並經主管機關核定優先順序。","observationEn":"Site practice: Handover contains each bent's pushover curve, failure-mode determination, as-built photos of hinge-zone reinforcement, coupler test reports and post-earthquake thresholds; where assessment shows shear failure before flexure, the pier enters the retrofit programme with priority approved by the owner agency.","failure":"注意干擾：評估若只用設計時的未退化剪力強度，會誤判舊橋墩為彎曲破壞而不需補強；1999 年 921 地震中台灣有約 102 座主要橋梁嚴重受損，提醒既有橋墩的韌性缺陷在強震前往往不被察覺。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using the undegraded shear strength misclassifies old piers as flexure-governed and not needing retrofit; in the 1999 Chi-Chi earthquake about 102 major bridges in Taiwan were badly damaged, a reminder that ductility deficiencies in existing piers often go unnoticed until a strong earthquake. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以竣工圖與現地取樣（鑽心強度、鋼筋掃描、局部打除確認箍筋與搭接）建立既有橋墩模型，進行推覆分析並同時繪出剪力需求與剪力容量隨位移的曲線，交點即破壞模式判斷依據；評估結果須經第二位工程師複核。","textEn":"Build the existing-pier model from as-built drawings and site sampling (core strengths, rebar scanning, local breakouts to confirm hoops and splices), run a pushover and plot shear demand and degrading shear capacity against displacement, using their intersection to identify the failure mode; a second engineer checks the assessment.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接文件應包含每座排架的推覆曲線、破壞模式判斷、塑鉸區配筋竣工照片、續接器試驗報告與震後檢查門檻；既有橋墩評估若顯示剪力先於彎曲破壞，須排入補強計畫並經主管機關核定優先順序。","textEn":"Handover contains each bent's pushover curve, failure-mode determination, as-built photos of hinge-zone reinforcement, coupler test reports and post-earthquake thresholds; where assessment shows shear failure before flexure, the pier enters the retrofit programme with priority approved by the owner agency.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「既有橋墩評估與工程交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Assessing existing piers and engineering handover\"?","options":["以竣工圖與現地取樣（鑽心強度、鋼筋掃描、局部打除確認箍筋與搭接）建立既有橋墩模型，進行推覆分析並同時繪出剪力需求與剪力容量隨位移的曲線，交點即破壞模式判斷依據。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","單調推到破壞的試驗就足以代表地震下的柱韌性。"],"optionsEn":["Build the existing-pier model from as-built drawings and site sampling (core strengths, rebar scanning, local breakouts to confirm hoops and splices), run a pushover and plot shear demand and degrading shear capacity against displacement, using their intersection to identify the failure mode.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A monotonic push to failure is enough to represent column ductility under earthquakes."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以竣工圖與現地取樣（鑽心強度、鋼筋掃描、局部打除確認箍筋與搭接）建立既有橋墩模型，進行推覆分析並同時繪出剪力需求與剪力容量隨位移的曲線，交點即破壞模式判斷依據；評估結果須經第二位工程師複核。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build the existing-pier model from as-built drawings and site sampling (core strengths, rebar scanning, local breakouts to confirm hoops and splices), run a pushover and plot shear demand and degrading shear capacity against displacement, using their intersection to identify the failure mode; a second engineer checks the assessment. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b047-v13-40","title":"既有橋墩評估與工程交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Assessing existing piers and engineering handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"prerequisiteIds":["b047-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「剪力隨韌性退化」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Shear degradation with ductility” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"評估若只用設計時的未退化剪力強度，會誤判舊橋墩為彎曲破壞而不需補強；1999 年 921 地震中台灣有約 102 座主要橋梁嚴重受損，提醒既有橋墩的韌性缺陷在強震前往往不被察覺。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using the undegraded shear strength misclassifies old piers as flexure-governed and not needing retrofit; in the 1999 Chi-Chi earthquake about 102 major bridges in Taiwan were badly damaged, a reminder that ductility deficiencies in existing piers often go unnoticed until a strong earthquake. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：評估流程是先求彎曲容量對應的剪力需求，再與隨韌性退化的剪力容量比較，判斷破壞模式；結果決定是否需要鋼板包覆或纖維複材補強，並寫入交接與維護文件。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Assessment first finds the shear demand corresponding to flexural capacity, then compares it with shear capacity degrading with ductility to identify the failure mode; the result decides whether steel or fibre-reinforced-polymer jacketing is needed and is written into handover and maintenance records.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「混凝土剪力強度是固定值，不會因柱子的彎曲變形而改變。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The concrete shear strength is a fixed value that does not change with column flexural deformation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b047-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"評估若只用設計時的未退化剪力強度，會誤判舊橋墩為彎曲破壞而不需補強；1999 年 921 地震中台灣有約 102 座主要橋梁嚴重受損，提醒既有橋墩的韌性缺陷在強震前往往不被察覺。","textEn":"Using the undegraded shear strength misclassifies old piers as flexure-governed and not needing retrofit; in the 1999 Chi-Chi earthquake about 102 major bridges in Taiwan were badly damaged, a reminder that ductility deficiencies in existing piers often go unnoticed until a strong earthquake.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]},{"id":"b047-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「既有橋墩評估與工程交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Assessing existing piers and engineering handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","評估若只用設計時的未退化剪力強度，會誤判舊橋墩為彎曲破壞而不需補強。","橋墩越強越好，所有構件都加強就能確保耐震安全。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Using the undegraded shear strength misclassifies old piers as flexure-governed and not needing retrofit.","The stronger the pier the better; strengthening every member guarantees seismic safety."],"answer":1,"explanation":"評估若只用設計時的未退化剪力強度，會誤判舊橋墩為彎曲破壞而不需補強；1999 年 921 地震中台灣有約 102 座主要橋梁嚴重受損，提醒既有橋墩的韌性缺陷在強震前往往不被察覺。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using the undegraded shear strength misclassifies old piers as flexure-governed and not needing retrofit; in the 1999 Chi-Chi earthquake about 102 major bridges in Taiwan were badly damaged, a reminder that ductility deficiencies in existing piers often go unnoticed until a strong earthquake. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v13s-caltrans-sdc-21","v13s-caltrans-sdc-17","v13s-peer-spd","v13s-wiki-cypress-viaduct","v13s-wiki-1999-jiji"],"curriculumVersion":13,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
